AH = {
    6: 'Fills the gap between work zone safety DT research and real-world deployment: LiDAR+radar+camera fusion validated with RTK-GNSS at a real work zone achieving lane-level accuracy, feeding a predictive DT framework pairing a Digital Shadow and Digital Sibling with TTC/PET conflict metrics and C-V2X warnings for proactive safety.',
    7: 'A perspective paper defining next-generation CPS and DT through two-way dynamic mapping between virtual models and the physical facility, distinguishing passive (model-based) from active (actuator-based) control, and illustrating scenarios: a teleoperated drywall robot controlled via wearable IMU motion capture, postural tracking with AR avatars and color-coded ergonomic risk feedback, and near-miss prediction using case-based reasoning and K-nearest neighbor.',
    13: 'Addresses the underexplored application of DT to fire safety management: a four-layer framework (physical building, virtual building, application, and user interaction layers) combining BIM, IoT, AI, data fusion, blockchain, and AR, with virtual-layer decisions fed back to the physical building layer for automatic control and operation optimization while keeping FM professionals in the loop.',
    14: 'Fills the gap between fire-safety DT research and operational emergency response: a functioning building DT (GUIDE2FR) fusing Wi-Fi/LoRa environmental beacons with live RTSP video in a Grafana plugin, plus an offline-trained ML forecasting pipeline (SVR, Huber, Random Forest, Gaussian Process, forward-chaining CV, adaptive ensemble) tested on data from four beacons during firefighter training exercises at Fire Station 9 in Madrid.',
    19: 'A standardization position paper reviewing DT definitions and frameworks and reporting the creation of CEN/TC 442/WG 9, whose 34-use-case technical report CEN/TR 18077 and the resulting European standard aim to give the built environment a shared DT definition; it grounds its argument in two implemented management platforms, the Bidebieta-Basauri railway station and the UPM civil engineering school.',
    20: 'Proposes a closed-loop conceptual model of DTs for construction sites, structured as three functional boxes: F1 data acquisition (IoT/RFID), F2 data analysis and simulation, and F3 BIM transformation into a web-based model; it is grounded in the empirical Smart Twins 4.0 system, which tracked 151 formwork panels with RFID and a web-based BIM, finding 100% external and 98% internal defects.',
    21: 'Addresses fragmented inspection data by replacing desktop photogrammetry with a serverless spatial intelligence hub: timeout-resilient orchestration of SfM/MVS, PostGIS-anchored defect records linked to georeferenced 3D meshes via raycasting and frustum-based image retrieval, end-to-end reconstruction in under one hour, sub-25 ms query latency, and over 90% image retrieval accuracy on two real UAV inspection datasets.',
    22: 'Demonstrates an operational digital twin for railway bridge SHM: low-cost wireless accelerometers (about EUR 300), hybrid edge-cloud processing with real-time FFT, unsupervised clustering of normal vibration, FEM-calibrated synthetic damage data, and a LightGBM classifier reaching ROC-AUC 0.9999 on two years of in-service vibration data from a bridge in the Basque Country.',
    23: 'Provides a methodology for integrating SHM with numerical DT models for seismic assessment of heritage buildings: a LiDAR-derived BIM of the Basilica Maria Auxiliadora in Lima fed calibrated SAP2000 and 3DEC models (about 4500 block elements, 161000 contact zones), modal analysis with 220 modes, time-history analysis reproducing the 2007 Pisco earthquake crack patterns, and 25 sensor control points selected via intensity-duration-frequency plots.',
    35: 'Derives a comprehensive requirements analysis for critical infrastructure crisis management and resilience and maps it onto a Digital Twin Conceptual Framework with four guiding principles (human-in-the-loop control, parsimony with accepted uncertainty, preparedness for complexity and emergence, safe experiments and training) plus a conceptual model of virtual replica, clones, toolbox, and control center.',
    42: 'Assigns ANNs two roles in a DT for SHM of reinforced concrete bridges: first, physically informed deep learning calibrates the virtual twin by identifying material parameters (E, fc, ft, fracture energy) from ATENA nonlinear finite element sensitivity analyses, demonstrated on a Leonhardt shear beam with datasets of 100, 400, and 1000 samples; second, the trained ANN serves as a fast-response surrogate for real-time engineering interpretation of monitoring data.',
    44: 'Provides a real ASHVIN H2020 pilot of digital twinning during construction of an RC office building in Barcelona: six independent information pipelines (crane hook IMU/GPS tracking with Random Forest activity recognition at 93.27% accuracy, slab post-tensioning strains, laser-scan deflection checks, concrete maturity temperatures, formwork vibration accelerations, mobile-app progress monitoring) feeding a knowledge-graph-based Unity dashboard.',
    45: 'Fills the gap between heritage-bridge conservation and quantitative risk assessment: on a 120-year-old Australian reinforced concrete bridge, ambient vibration testing with ten wireless accelerometers plus laser displacement sensing feeds a Spacegass finite-element digital twin validated against measured natural frequencies (20.15 Hz versus 19.51 Hz, 3.2 percent difference), then used for what-if simulations of overweight vehicles and foundation scour.',
    46: 'Closes the automation gap between rebar reconstruction, segmentation, dimensional inspection and issue tracking: a GoPro-based SfM-MVS pipeline with AprilTag scale calibration builds a semantically enriched 3D model, Mask R-CNN plus DBSCAN segment rebars, and Scan-vs-BIM comparison identifies and tracks defects, reaching over 90 percent precision, over 97 percent recall, 95.5 percent diameter accuracy for large rebars and 0.98 percent mean relative spacing error.',
    47: 'Fills the sparse-point surrogate gap for tunnel digital twins: the DF-STTN hybrid surrogate, pairing Swin Transformer and TabTransformer with dual-stage fusion, predicts full-field ground settlement and lining deformation for shield tunnels under adjacent excavation, trained on 1000 parametric finite-element samples and reaching R2 0.9898 and 0.9951, outperforming six baseline networks, with genetic-algorithm back-analysis estimating soil parameters within 4 percent error.',
    49: 'Addresses the reactive and static gap in tunnel construction emergency response: a digital twin continuously integrating settlement, TBM operational and structural monitoring data is coupled with a knowledge graph using SWRL rule-based reasoning to infer hazards, detect anomalies and suggest mitigations, with inference results visualized back in the twin; deployed on an urban tunnel project in Shanghai where it enabled early anomaly identification.',
    50: 'Addresses robust parallel control of construction equipment under uncertainty: a mobile gin pole digital twin for UHV construction embeds finite-element kinetic analysis with a TROA-ET surrogate model (R2 0.9642) and NSGA-III safety-efficiency optimisation within a DT parallel-control architecture supported by bidirectional 4G and MQTT links.',
    61: 'Fills the group-level gap in bridge digital twins: for a regional bridge network around Shanghai, weigh-in-motion and multi-source machine vision fusion measure full-bridge traffic loads on a target bridge, lightweight sensors capture responses on group bridges, and measured loads drive mechanical models in digital space, enabling working-condition perception and safety warning across the whole network, demonstrated with Monte Carlo and Intelligent Driver Model simulations on the Yongjiang cable-stayed bridge.',
    65: 'Fills the incident-response gap of subway station digital twins: interconnected per-station twins process camera, microphone and sensor data in a fog computing environment, a fine-tuned YOLOv8 detector (mAP 0.5 of 92.4 percent) spots events shown on a mobile app with a voice assistant, and personnel response times improved by 17.4 percent versus the REPEAT platform across 50 simulated trials.',
    66: 'Responds to the lack of practical construction risk models: DTCRAM combines a three-round Delphi study with nine industry experts, identifying 15 construction risks and 15 countermeasures classified into 12 strategy types, with a five-layer digital twin structure (physical twin, data twin, twin model, data analysis, decision feedback) for dynamic monitoring and risk prediction, verified on the Thames Tidal Tunnel case with over 1 percent probability reduction per project.',
    67: 'Synthesizes 146 bridge disaster management articles to expose fragmented technology integration, delayed response and poor coordination, then proposes the RtBDM framework combining dynamic adaptation, digitalisation and a disaster-cycle component that integrates BIM and digital twin technologies with sensors, big data analytics, IoT and artificial intelligence for real-time monitoring, early warning, response and recovery across pre-disaster to post-disaster phases.',
    68: 'Addresses static, code-bound multi-robot scheduling: a closed-loop digital twin in Unity, synchronized with ROS and Gazebo, supports integer-programming task allocation whose constraints are updated by an LLM interpreting plain-language site narratives, achieving over 97 percent constraint and parameter extraction accuracy with GPT-4.1, optimal plans within about one second and 0.08-second replanning across 1024 scenarios of 27 tasks and 15 robots.',
    72: 'Fills the renovation-phase gap in digital twins: a stakeholder-informed Renovation Digital Twin built with Design Science Research in the RINNO project monitors 13 KPIs across cost, schedule, quality, safety and environment on the Project Sarrazins demo site in Lille, and a Technology Acceptance Model survey of 102 professionals gave attitude toward use RII 0.894 while the site achieved a 73 percent emissions reduction.',
    74: 'Diagnoses the standardization gap in AEC digital twins through a systematic review of 229 publications (2016 to 2021) from four databases, showing DTs remain application-driven and vendor-dependent, then proposes a conceptual DT development framework built on the ISO 19650 series: PIM and AIM information containers federated in a CDE, IoT and WSN monitoring, and machine learning for decisions and actuator actions.',
    76: 'Demonstrates location-enabled construction digital twins on a live Skanska highway project, building health and safety and progress monitoring twins in Unreal Engine 5 with CesiumJS georeferencing. The health and safety twin delivers site walk-throughs, clickable asset inspection records, color-coded hazard and risk boxes, and 1-metre danger-zone alerts around machinery built with no-code Blueprints.',
    78: 'Fills the behavioral-psychology gap in worker unsafe-behavior research by building a closed-loop hybrid simulation digital twin in AnyLogic that couples agent-based, system dynamics and discrete-event models with dual attitude theory and reinforcement learning. Calibrated with 84 valid questionnaires (Cronbach alpha 0.868), experiments with 84 worker agents show proactive management sustains safety after withdrawal while reactive management decays fast.',
    84: 'Establishes an adaptable methodology for existing-bridge digital twins addressing software obsolescence and interoperability: laser-scanned geometry (RIEGL VZ-2000i) converted to IFC 4.3 BIM and enriched from the KUBA database, then imported into SCIA Engineer for what-if corrosion scenarios on the 377.60 m Praz bridge and DE-algorithm FE updating against DIC measurements on the Grandson bridge.',
    86: 'Combines a digital twin construction-safety model with a PSO-optimized BP neural network for vibration displacement sensing and recognition of large structures: the twin generates real-time structural state training samples and the model reaches 98.2 percent prediction accuracy overall, 99.1 percent for tension-cable stress, with eigenvalue EV 0.978 and correct critical-component identification on a 48 m span steel roof model.',
    88: 'Integrates WebGIS (Cesium), WebBIM (Xeokit) and graph algorithms (Neo4j) in a three-layer bridge DT with a common data environment, JSON-based defect modeling and triple-based roadmap graphs, enabling real-time monitoring, drone inspection, traffic diversion and maintenance planning; validated on the River Neath Swing Bridge with regional operation and individual maintenance case studies.',
    92: 'Proposes a Bayesian-network system digital twin for county-scale life-cycle risk assessment of bridge networks, fusing NBI inspection ratings, traffic monitoring and river gage data across 1,034 bridges, 1,261 traffic stations and 10 river gages in Miami-Dade County, with a 6,478-node, 10,584-edge graph capturing component, system and cross-system correlations for scenario-based risk updating.',
    97: 'Addresses the real-time human-robot communication gap in timber frame construction: a vision-based collaborative robot interprets the layout marks drawn by a carpenter as cutting operations, and a robot digital twin shown through HoloLens 2 mixed reality previews all motions, danger zones and collision warnings so the carpenter can safely time entry to the collaborative workspace under ISO/TS 15066.',
    100: 'Combines deterministic and probabilistic methods into a four-stage holistic condition-assessment concept for fatigue-loaded railway noise barriers: standard fatigue calculations, visual condition classes linked with monitoring data, finite-element digital twin studies of bolt-post installation conditions, and Bayesian updating of reliability and remaining service life, grounded in large-scale fatigue tests with Austrian Federal Railways.',
    102: 'Builds a metaverse-based evacuation training system where a rainbow DQN agent learns dynamic guidance-sign strategies from a social-force crowd simulation of a teaching building; sensors such as cameras and smoke detectors would supply real-time crowd and disaster data to cloud servers. In two simulated scenes the agent balances exits and reduces evacuation time versus static signs and shortest-path guidance.',
    104: 'Closes the perception-to-execution gap on a real high-rise self-climbing platform project: Component-ID plus timestamp aligns video, sensor, BIM and text streams; a multimodal Transformer recognizes operation states and predicts short-horizon risks; constraint-encoded policies generate feasible task sequences delivered via AR with acknowledgments, raising warning lead time from 1.8 to 4.6 seconds and cutting violations by 52 percent.',
    106: 'Proposes a sky-space-ground digital twin framework fusing RBIM with SSIoT multi-source sensing, including real-time LiDAR, automated monitoring robots, GNSS and SBAS-InSAR settlement data, linked through GUID object mapping tables and a cloud platform with weighted-average fusion and conflict detection, achieving consistent millimeter and sub-millimeter settlement precision across monitoring points.',
    109: 'Brings crowdsourced visual data into a digital twin city for risk-informed decision-making: 135 smartphone photos from five participants localize distant vulnerable objects via mean-shift clustering, achieving average distance errors of 4.49 metres at ranges of 18.6 to 38.7 metres, and the updated Houston city model is shown in a CAVE for interactive visualization of hazard cascades.',
    110: 'Fills the gap between macro city-level twin frameworks and single-phase pipeline platforms with a full-cycle BIM0 to BIM6 plus lightweight BIM-GIS architecture for the Shanghai Oriental Hub; a 5-month pilot deployed 28 IoT nodes (pressure, gas leakage, surface temperature) with under 1 s delay, raising planning collision detection from 68 to 97 percent and predicting one valve aging risk 7 days in advance.',
    111: 'Addresses the lack of real-time worker authorization verification in large open construction sites: a UAV digital twin framework at CUHK combining YOLOv10-LCA detection (mAP50 raised from 31.5 to 96.4 percent, 3 ms inference), DeepSORT tracking, georegistered 3D site reconstruction and GPS electronic work permits, validated across Hong Kong construction projects with 19 inspection sites routed by 3D-TSP within a 41-minute flight limit.',
    112: 'Targets delayed hoisting control and fragmented information in modular integrated construction stacking: a DT platform (DTPTS) fusing UWB and IMU sensing with a PosTraFormer spatio-temporal network whose multi-layer GCNs model trajectory point relations, achieving the lowest FDE and ADE across four lifting scenarios (0.0417 and 0.0476 in lifting) and on a real PolyU site case after fine-tuning (0.0277 and 0.0319), with protective collision shields in the twin.',
    115: 'Brings bidirectional cyber-physical interaction to construction machinery where literature is scarce: a laboratory prototype of an AR and digital twin CPS using an Arduino Uno and Yun sensor and actuator net (HC-SR04 ultrasonic, MPU-6050 inertial) on a tower crane analogue, with a Unity3D server relaying serial data to a marker-based AR controller at 0.25 s command latency and a DT animation lag of 0.5 to 1.0 s.',
    118: 'Bridges the gap between deterministic block theory and hours-long high-fidelity simulations with the Universal Discontinuity Index, a probabilistic score fusing physical damage, effective stress intensity, active fracture ratio and kinematic feasibility; it reproduced progressive batch failure in milliseconds versus BPDEM and FDEM, and on 52 El Teniente faces with 5300 DFN-KBT realizations predicted unstable block counts at R2 of 0.93 and 95 percent accuracy, feeding a Poisson early-warning model.',
    121: 'Fills the scarcity of whole-lifecycle intelligent monitoring for deep foundation pits with an integrated approach at Waterlands Resort East Station on Shenzhen Metro Line 12: three-dimensional transparent geology, MEMS, BOFDA distributed fiber, UAV and machine vision sensing, four neural network predictors with GA-BP performing best, plus a BIM monitoring platform and Unity3D digital twin app with AR for construction and maintenance phases.',
    122: 'Extends the Digital Twin for Construction Safety concept with a Right-time Analysis and Mitigation module tested at a Munich railway maintenance staging area: safeBIM rule checking plus RTK-GNSS over LoRa tracking at 1.0 cm median and 2.3 cm 95th percentile precision, detecting 99 unauthorized entries, mapping telehandler blind spots (right side obstructed to 1.9 m) and computing safety-weighted walkway routes that informed a revised safeBIM plan.',
    125: 'Fills the absence of a construction-machinery-specific digital twin maturity model: five dimensions and 24 indicators across five levels, built from literature and expert interviews, assessed by Louvain expert grouping plus a penalty-weighted bi-objective opinion aggregation; applied to an automated construction system, the framework located the twin at Level 3, with continuous learning and real-time data processing scoring only Level 2.',
    128: 'Addresses offline processing, uncertain sensor data quality and missing structural-analysis knowledge in BIM-based SHM with a digital twin framework tested on a prototyped aluminum frame at NJIT: Robot Structural Analysis guides sensor placement, Raspberry Pi sensing with strain gauge and laser distance sensor, wavelet sym4 denoising (threshold 25, level 6), and Revit Dynamo color-coded deformation visualization refreshing at 5 Hz from one sensor via bending-moment interpolation.',
    129: 'Targets sparse and lagging manual tunnel monitoring with an IoT plus digital twin system on a shield tunnel beneath the Jinan High-Speed Train Depot: multi-source fusion of personnel, pipe-sheet, shield and environmental data into BIM dynamic modeling, improved D-S evidence theory with conflict weakening and a validity factor cutting belief interval length 0.37 to 0.14, capturing a palm face collapse; prediction errors under 1.9 MN thrust and 5.44 mm settlement.',
    137: 'Fills the gap of preliminary clearance checking without field surveys: a digital twin method reconstructing the existing main road and underpass road from online map data (Digimap DSM, DTM and aerial photos) via road-marking extraction, smoothing-spline alignment fitting at R-square near 1.0, and flattened terrain models; clash detection of a 5.338 m clearance envelope in the M11 and Sawbridgeworth Road case caught insufficient clearance and guided redesign of underpass vertical alignment.',
    138: 'Provides automatic monitoring for arch cover method subway stations, rare in the literature, via a DT and IoT system at Shikui Road Station of Dalian Metro Line 5: pressure cells, rebar meters, strain gauges and displacement meters stream into a Revit secondary-developed BIM platform with IFC-extended sensor attributes and color-change alarms; lining pressure rises after temporary support removal informed inverse analysis that set midwall demolition at 12 m.',
    141: 'Fills the gap between BIM and IoT fire monitoring and closed-loop fire protection control: a BFP ontology fuses static BIM geometry with dynamic IoT sensing data into a DT data model, and rule models plus BPMN process models execute intelligent control with update rules keeping virtual and physical spaces synchronized. Three scenarios, sprinkler, fire door, and smoke control, were verified through FDS simulation.',
    143: 'Addresses the scarcity of experimental knowledge on unsafe hoisting behavior effects: a human-machine interaction DT built on a 1/30 scale tower crane with 20 Hz sensors synchronizes virtual FEM and BIM models through IoT data flow, and incremental dynamic load analysis yields collapse probability levels (TCL, FCL, MCL, JCL, CCL, RCL) showing tilt hoisting as most dangerous with foundation and masts most vulnerable.',
    144: 'Fills the construction-phase early-warning gap for unsafe hoisting operations: a DT mirrors a 1:80 scaled tower crane through STM32 boards, three 9-axis IMUs, two laser sensors, and MQTT, and a standards-derived knowledge graph built from seven standards and 86 accident reports identifies safety events, achieving over 70 percent warning accuracy with under 20 percent false alarms and Theil consistency below 0.1.',
    148: 'Addresses the cognitive overload and information silos that block adoption of automated safety analysis: a safety ontology and Prolog knowledge graph capture BIM, schedule, and hazard analysis results (about 3,800 nodes and 20,000 edges), and categorized query building blocks turn seven planning questions into queries answered in under one second, revealing cross-domain impacts of crew assignment and delivery changes on safety.',
    154: 'Systematizes pre-hurricane preparedness beyond error-prone manual checklist inspection: SfM and MVS photogrammetry reconstruct jobsite point clouds, ResNet50 semantic segmentation reaches 98.2 percent accuracy, and a depth-aware projection raises 3D segmentation accuracy from 97.85 to 99.8 percent; volumetric measurement of nine material piles (errors 2.4 to 9.2 percent) feeds kinetic-energy threat heatmaps at hurricane-category wind speeds.',
    155: 'Extends jobsite debris risk assessment to neighboring communities: a geometric digital twin of a railroad jobsite gravel pile built from 45 UAV images (volumetric error about 4.6 percent) feeds a HAZUS-based glazing reliability model together with ResNet50 street-view window segmentation (85.0 percent accuracy), computing failure probability of nearby dwelling glazing systems across 35 to 65 m/s wind scenarios.',
    158: 'Fills the worker safety and training gap in underground utility tunnel management: a LiDAR-modeled UUT digital twin in Unreal is coupled with a four-degree-of-freedom motion platform, visual and kinematic acceleration control, and treadmill velocity thresholding to reduce cybersickness; SSQ-based tests with 17 participants show significantly reduced headaches and motion sickness, with MANOVA confirming the technique effect.',
    163: 'Fills the scarce real-world evidence gap on building safety DTs with two 17-month deployments: an office and a grain drying facility using Raspberry Pi sensor packages (thermal, RGB, UV, motion sensors), LiDAR-derived dimensionally accurate 3D models in Unity and WebGL, and Azure dashboards; normal operational signature analysis detects anomalies, localizes fires without triangulation, and a candle flame was detected in under one second.',
    165: 'Fills the gap for structures under simultaneous seismic and arbitrary loads: a 3D-printed MECOS benchmark pipe on a shaking table with an actuator, an updated ANSYS finite element model, and a Craig-Bampton reduced order model (62 DOFs, about one percent of the 7,428-DOF model) yield about 450 times faster calculation, enabling real-time estimation of unmeasured responses and loads with RMSE 0.0103 and 0.0266 versus sensors.',
    167: 'Overcomes the point-measurement limits of black-globe thermometers: UAV photogrammetry builds a geometric site twin, an on-site weather station streams temperature, humidity, irradiance, and wind, and SOLWEIG microclimate simulation with shadow, sky view factor, and surface material maps yields site-wide heat risk maps; in Stephenville, Texas, the simulation method estimated mean radiant temperature with RMSE 4.21 C and R2 0.93 versus 11.80 C and 0.44 for the black-globe method.',
    168: 'Bridges pre-simulated fire knowledge and real-time emergency response: an edge-layer informative digital twin on a cloud-edge-device architecture compares live sensor data against a pre-simulated fire knowledge base using online DTW with parallel processing, recognizing fire scenarios in 0.88 s versus over eight hours of CFD; zone-based ARET, RRET, and safety margin assessment cut evacuation time by 65 s and injuries by 406 in a Hoehyeon underground mall simulation.',
    176: 'Fills the real-time cost versus accuracy gap between mechanistic and statistical twins: a multi-fidelity surrogate combining a low-fidelity RBF trained on large low-fidelity data with a high-fidelity RBF on few high-fidelity samples yields a lightweight crane boom twin predicting stress and deformation in 0.035 s with R2 above 0.98 at 18 test points, plus Gaussian uncertainty quantification from 140 repeated lifts, rendered in a WebGL scene.',
    178: 'Addresses the gap between component-level computer vision damage detection and whole-building post-earthquake safety assessment: a BIM-referenced digital twin where the BIM guides automatic selection of optimal UAV images per damage-sensitive component, GrabCut-based segmentation assigns each pixel to a BIM element (IoU 0.80 to 0.90), and 3D point cloud change detection flags damaged nonstructural components, demonstrated on Turner Hall with 989 images and a synthetic masonry damage environment.',
    181: 'Fills the gap of automated condition monitoring for pitched slated roofs, for which no prior orthophoto or segmentation work existed: a pipeline generating occlusion-free metric panel orthophotos from SfM reconstruction plus the building DT model, then deep-learning semantic segmentation into slate, leadwork and other, with PointRend plus background label correction reaching 94.22 mIoU and 100 percent background accuracy, validated on Duff House, St Marys Church and a Stirling house.',
    183: 'Turns noisy laser point clouds of large-diameter pipelines into a geometric digital twin enabling quantitative condition assessment, closing the gap between raw scanning and deformation measurement: LMedS slice-center fitting, DBSCAN clustering with Gaussian fitting and density-based region growing achieve sub-millimeter mean error against total station truth, with ovality and blockage quantified via OI and VI indicators at only 7 percent of KDE runtime.',
    185: 'Addresses the vulnerability of physical sensors in dredger construction safety control: a digital twin-driven virtual sensor trained on real SCADA data (793 dimensions) from the Tongcheng hopper dredger at Tianjin Port, using Lasso plus random forest feature selection and Savitzky-Golay filtering, with DBN (R2 0.987) outperforming LSTM, XGBoost and SVR, and residual-based warning within a 99 percent confidence interval to diagnose torsional vibration faults.',
    194: 'Fills the synchronization gap between BIM and FEM in construction-phase cable structures: multi-stage laser scanning (six scans of an 18-cable-set cable net) feeds parametric IFC modeling and ABAQUS secondary-development FEM, with BIM-to-point-cloud accuracy of 15 to 20 mm, per-stage modeling and computation within 140 s, and FEM prediction deviations of cable shape and force versus next-stage measurements within about 1 and 2 percent.',
    195: 'Closes the gap between industrial speed-and-separation monitoring and seamless construction worker-robot collaboration: a digital twin system perceiving workers via Azure Kinect 32-point skeletons with 14 capsule representations, robots via URDF plus encoders, and materials via ArUco and QR tags with IFC data, computing rapid separation distance and dynamic protective separation distance to halt the robot, achieving 9.8 FPS, 0.177 s reaction and 0.09 m perception error with zero collisions in static and dynamic conflict tests.',
    196: 'Fills the planning gap for WSN and BIM integration in garage environmental monitoring: a working digital twin system with Zigbee mesh nodes (MQ-7 CO and DHT-11 temperature and humidity) that react to simulated hazardous gas within 1 to 2 s, automatically switching on ventilator and flashing alarm, with 250 m direct and over 450 m relayed communication, color-coded BIM visualization via Navisworks API, and roughly 40 percent cost saving versus handheld detectors.',
    203: 'Elevates prefabricated hoisting digital twin research from static expert-based risk scoring to the essence of safety risk: a DEMATEL-ISM hierarchical risk model embedded in the twin, with Bayesian network reasoning via EM-trained parameters computing the key degree of indirect inducement factors when a direct factor such as sling angle turns dangerous, verified on a 71,172 square meter Tianjin prefabricated project with RFID, IMU, crane black box and LoRa sensing.',
    204: 'Fills the coupling-analysis vacancy in hoisting safety: a digital twin framework combining IoT and BIM with Apriori association-rule mining (support 0.5, confidence 0.6, lift-ranked rules) mapped into a weighted complex network whose degree centrality identifies key risk nodes such as illegal operation and poor safety-protection wearing, validated on a large prefabricated project using 26 days of integrated site records.',
    205: 'Moves digital twin application beyond reflecting reality toward virtual control of reality for cable tensioning: a fusion mechanism of digital twins and AI with multi-dimensional and multi-scale twin agents, a DBN (RBM pretraining plus BP fine-tuning) predicting cable forces, and a 1:10 wheel-spoke cable truss test where twin correction against sensor strain cut cable-force errors to within 3 percent and DBN-based safety levels guided maintenance under quarter-span live load.',
    207: 'Addresses the lack of efficient impact response prediction tools for structure O and M: a high-fidelity digital twin combining BIM, 3D laser scanning and ANSYS/LS-DYNA simulation, with an improved LM-BP neural network (14 inputs, 5 outputs) trained on 219 drop-hammer working conditions, achieving R of 0.99293 in training and 0.98766 in testing with 99.7 percent overall accuracy, versus 48 hours of physical testing.',
    208: 'Addresses the disconnect between independent indoor safety systems and building information: a digital twin-based indoor safety management system combining lightweight WebGL BIM, LoRa IoT terminals (oxygen, CO, smoke, temperature, door and window sensors plus camera people counting) and SVM models that classify fire, illegal intrusion and overcrowding with 97.57 to 100 percent accuracy and grade danger levels at 96.2 percent accuracy with R2 above 0.89, applied to a Beijing Winter Olympics stadium building.',
    210: 'Fills the gap between finite-element simulation and next-moment stress prediction during overall jacking of an airport terminal steel mesh roof: a digital twin built with Midas/Gen life-and-death element analysis guides sensor placement on twelve hydraulic jacks and key bars, and an XGBoost model predicts key-bar stress with 98 percent accuracy and validation R2 of 0.9919, outperforming GA-BPNN and random forest.',
    211: 'Fills the gap of costly experience-based health monitoring for large-span steel mesh frames by combining a digital twin with geometric, finite-element, behavioral and rule models with random forest feature-importance analysis of overall jacking data from an airport project, showing that maximum jacking height difference and jacking speed dominate structural stress, consistent with construction code provisions.',
    219: 'Fills the gap between conceptual community-resilience digital twins and functional visualization: COWINE uses Cities:Skylines as simulation engine integrated with real-world topography, infrastructure, economic, traffic and disaster data for a Brevard County Florida pilot region, with interactive visualizations and a tornado case study demonstrating collaborative before-during-after resilience planning among stakeholders.',
    221: 'Fills the gap of resource-intensive modeling blocking city-scale slope digital twins: DrainNet, a CNN with directional convolutions, dilated blocks and channel attention, delineates drainage channels with 81.26 percent Dice and 0.24 connectivity error using only 0.28M parameters on the 1226-image CurvaChannel dataset, and an automated Grasshopper workflow builds slope BIM models about nine times faster than Dynamo for a web-based twin platform.',
    225: 'Bridges defect-based inspection classification and performance forecasting for tunnel lifecycle management: a 2D classified-cell grid converts visual inspection data into tunnel serviceability index values, inverse exponential limit analysis validated against stochastic literature models yields a 16-year target intervention time, and an inspection digital twin of railway tunnel TL 01 attaches metadata through EleFront with online photo links.',
    226: 'Automates tunnel inspection digital twin creation from heterogeneous field data: point clouds from a Faro Focus 3D X330 scan of the Coastal Tunnel are cleaned and decimated, meshed by Poisson reconstruction in Grasshopper, with the new MDQ index guiding mesh quality, and metadata attached via EleFront; digital inspection took about 18 minutes versus 46 minutes manual and located a leakage the visual survey missed.',
    235: 'Addresses fragmented document-based management of a diffused university asset: a BIM-GIS web platform integrates spatial and functional data from several directorates into a centralized relational database with a tailor-made space encoding, feeding an interactive 3D map with analytical dashboards for two University of Turin demonstrator buildings, plus crowd simulation to assess fire evacuation safety levels.',
    238: 'Fills the underexplored gap of hyperparameter optimization in serverless decentralized federated learning: local SMAC tuning with performance-weighted one-shot aggregation on six Raspberry Pi nodes cut worker-safety convergence rounds from 42 to 18 and MAE from 0.058 to 0.042, and MNIST rounds from 8 to 3 with 95.3 percent accuracy, while a digital twin layer provides observability without centralizing data.',
    239: 'Fills the lack of integrated multi-worker safety monitoring systems by coupling a digital twin platform with federated learning: six Raspberry Pi edge nodes train a DNN on 50,000 records of worker, weather and structural data, and a normal-distribution-based dynamic node selection improves FedAVG aggregation to R2 0.978 under IID and 0.965 under non-IID conditions with 0.551 s average inference delay.',
    247: 'Reconceptualizes construction defects as latent energy and carbon drivers: the Quality-Sustainability Integration Index combines severity, carbon and repair frequency calibrated from 83 professionals, 14 Lagos buildings and 847 repair entries, showing waterproofing defects carry a 3.4x carbon multiplier and 82.3 tCO2e per 1000 m2 over five years, with a 44 percent lifecycle carbon gap between high and poor quality scenarios.',
    253: 'Maps the under-reviewed use of ontologies and semantic web technologies for construction execution: a systematic review of 52 papers from Scopus and Web of Science spanning 2005-2023 categorizes use cases including safety management, compliance checking, site monitoring and 4D BIM, analyzes how semantic web tools support BIM and digital twin applications, and positions ontologies as the path toward BIM Maturity Stage 3.',
    254: 'Fills the gap between geometric UAV reconstructions and semantically understood damage: the AEDT framework fuses multiview UAV imagery, SfM 3D reconstruction and a MobileNetV2-based CNN with 81 percent test accuracy and macro F1 0.81 into a GIS-compatible interactive twin of a Taiwan soil and water conservation structure, cutting on-site inspection time from 3.5 to 1.3 hours and linking anomalies to maintenance records.',
    255: 'Fills the gap of enriching geometric building twins with electrical and fire-safety objects that prior scan-to-BIM methods ignored: a mostly automated pipeline fusing laser scanning and photogrammetry, with Mask-RCNN detections mapped into point clouds via COLMAP, ICP alignment and voxel raycasting, then RANSAC shape fitting and OCR text extraction, raising mIoU for smoke alarms from 29.1% to 48.6% and lights from 69.4% to 79.9% versus KPConv.',
    262: 'Proposes a BIM-enhanced digital twin architecture for construction pollution management in building renovation, defined by five components (physical entities, virtual models, DT data, services, connections) and a hybrid LOIN-LOD framework specifying minimum modelling requirements; a Chulalongkorn University auditorium pilot integrated six IoT sensor clusters (noise, PM2.5, CO2, vibration) with MQTT, Firebase, Node-RED threshold alerts and a React plus Forge dashboard, with 1-second data transmission.',
    265: 'Explains a satellite monitoring failure on the Ponte della Musica arch bridge in Rome using a 3D FEM digital twin in SAP2000 calibrated against ambient vibration tests (three experimental eigenfrequencies 0.92, 1.01 and 1.33 Hz reproduced within about 2% error); thermo-mechanical analyses show a most probable plus or minus 5 degrees C variation causes about 2 cm of deck displacement, exceeding the X-band line-of-sight measurement limit of roughly 0.8 cm.',
    271: 'Presents a LiDAR-simulated digital twin approach generating probabilistic 3D point clouds of rail fasteners in real time from grayscale and depth images via a Siamese self-supervised contrastive network (vision transformer, Fourier network, multilevel fusion) and a Bayesian neural network; trained on structured-light data from a 10 km/h track inspection vehicle, it reaches a Chamfer distance of 0.3926 and Hausdorff distance of 1063.79 with noise augmentation, followed by RANSAC segmentation and cubic interpolation.',
    273: 'Couples IFC-based BIM semantics with mobile crowd sensing for real-time evacuation routing: IFC entities become a dynamic decision graph updated by Wi-Fi RSSI localization using a two-stage strategy that also infers silent users, and an extended Dijkstra algorithm with AHP-derived weights (distance, time, exit availability, route safety index) recomputes paths; field tests in a four-story academic building under three scenarios reached 94 to 96% in-time evacuation and 3.02 to 3.58 m positioning error.',
    278: 'Integrates BIM, FEM and real-time monitoring to assess seismic behavior of the Prince Moulay Abdellah Dam in Morocco: a Revit model with sensor metadata feeds a MIDAS FEA NX 3D soil-structure model (278,778 tetrahedral elements) via Parasolid export, and response-spectrum analyses show maximum tensile stresses around 12% and compressive stresses around 85% of allowable limits at 0.5 g; vinchon records from the September 2023 magnitude 6.8 earthquake confirm abutments displace more than the stable central vault.',
    283: 'Develops a conceptual risk systematization for the Digital Twin for Construction Projects (DTCP) approach through READ-method document analysis of 32 selected studies, mapping five construction risk categories (planning and monitoring, security and safety, quality, human resources, execution) onto twin capabilities, and proposing a ten-step risk treatment procedure plus a custom risk matrix with reduced assessment levels to speed anomaly handling and prediction.',
    292: 'Delivers a BIM-based digital twin framework for urban roads in Turin integrating MMS LiDAR point clouds, municipal GIS layers and authoritative geodatabases into IFC 4.3 models at LoD200 (city scale) and LoD400 (asset scale), covering about 45 km of network with over 2000 vertical elements and achieving RMSE 3 cm geometric accuracy validated by cloud-to-mesh deviation analysis, creating AI-ready, semantically enriched datasets for maintenance planning.',
    297: 'Builds an intelligent overall planning model for underground space using a five-dimensional digital twin, analytic hierarchy process with variable weights and a Bayesian network for safety accident risk assessment; twin-based construction simulation yields a maximum column-bottom settlement of 21.897 mm and adjacent column differential of 2.886 mm, within code limits, and fire-scene imaging experiments show fused short-wave plus long-wave infrared equipment performs best under dense smoke.',
    298: 'Proposes a five-dimensional digital twin framework with six modules and a seven-step methodology for large underground cavern stability, adding IFC extensions (new entities and property sets for geotechnical monitoring, excavation sequence and convergence) and validated on the Neelum Jhelum hydropower powerhouse cavern where 52 extensometers, load cells and 24 prism targets feed FEM models to trigger rock support adjustments in near real time.',
    299: 'Develops an AI-enhanced digital twin for flood-driven roadway serviceability that couples flood simulation with a graph attention network predicting traffic speed 45 minutes ahead from 5-minute INRIX speed data and 6-hour flood intervals, using dynamic edges that appear and disappear with inundation to capture indirect impacts on non-flooded segments; validated on Hurricane Harvey traffic for two Houston zones, with flood edge features reducing prediction MSE.',
    300: 'Proposes reverse digital twin mapping of building envelope anomalies from UAV infrared point clouds: a PCRNet-based fusion model adds depth information for irregular geometries and a CNN detector classifies thermal anomalies, achieving 92% average accuracy, 96.3% precision, 94% recall and a 95.1% F1 score across 299 data points at 5.21 seconds per item, with anomalies registered into a digital twin model through Mask R-CNN markers for object-oriented management.',
    302: 'Fills the gap between real-time monitoring data and numerical simulation for slope safety: a stacking ensemble surrogate model (BP, RF, XGBoost, SVR, RBF) with multidimensional error analysis and adaptive parameter optimization predicts full-field displacement from limited monitoring points, reducing prediction error from 20 percent to 5 percent and reconstructing the 2010-2022 acceleration-stabilization deformation of the Donglingxin landslide at rates of 12.5-15.5-11.8 mm/y.',
    308: 'Addresses the gap between robotic facade inspection and quantitative, real-time damage assessment: a negative-pressure wall-climbing robot with RTK-GNSS and IMU localization feeds a lightweight YOLO12 segmentation model (0.775 mAP) whose skeletonization and PCA quantification reach 1.140 cm length error and 0.826 cm center error, all mapped into a cloud digital twin with 2.8-4.8 s response cycles on a Tongzhou Beijing building.',
    309: 'Fills the insufficient-data gap in deep-learning fault diagnosis of construction-robot joints: a gear-dynamics virtual entity generates faultless vibration data as the X-domain and a CycleGAN-based digital twin maps it to the physical Y-domain, so that with only 400 measured samples a CNN-ResNet classifier reaches 98.86 percent accuracy versus 32.5 percent without augmentation, outperforming GAN baselines on an RV reducer test rig.',
    313: 'Extends GIS-based heatwave vulnerability mapping into a graph-based urban digital twin: Google Solar API heat-index data, Vienna open population datasets and OpenStreetMap roads are fused into a dependency-risk graph whose centrality analysis identifies cumulative risk paths and critical blocks, including cold-spot node 683, and plans first-responder ambulance routes from cooling spots to high-risk populations, with sensitivity checks showing Spearman correlations near 0.8.',
    315: 'Fills the construction-phase gap left by operation-focused bridge digital twins: a multi-resolution digital twin for the Zhanlin Yellow River cable-stayed bridge links a web-BIM model with a Midas Civil finite element model (267 elements, 19 launching stages) and 120 strain gauges, applying standardized stress and deformation warning thresholds that triggered Level 1 and Level 2 alarms during jacking at 573 m.',
    318: 'Closes the data-model-decision loop for geological uncertainty ahead of tunnel faces: TEM, GPR and borehole data become point-cloud models of water content, lithology and integrity via KNN interpolation, and a fuzzy cloud probability model quantifies uncertainty to classify surrounding rock per meter within a 30 m range, achieving 92.95 percent accuracy across 539 exposed-rock records of five tunnels on the Tongji iS3 platform.',
    320: 'Fills the spatiotemporal risk-prognosis gap in foundation pit excavation: a five-component digital twin (physical space, FLAC3D virtual model, twin data, service, connections) fuses RFID, displacement, soil-pressure and environmental sensing to update an 850141-cell finite element model after each step, with Markov-chain risk prediction and a bow-tie model selecting control measures, validated on the Wuhan Metro Line 7 air-shaft pit with 15.2 mm maximum settlement.',
    321: 'Fills the gap between data-driven bridge SHM and expert knowledge: the DK-DTM framework combines UAV imagery processed by YOLOv8, LiDAR point clouds processed by PointNet, and LSTM-forecast sensor series with a fuzzy-logic expert knowledge base and rule engine, applied to the 612 m Hedong Bridge where it found a 12 mm mid-span displacement and early-stage fatigue risks.',
    322: 'Bridges the divide between data-driven automation with limited interpretability and human-centered assessment with limited scalability: a human-AI-knowledge HITL-DT framework formalizes engineering codes and human cognition (individual perception, team situation awareness) alongside AI reasoning into a closed-loop device-model-decision architecture for risk sensing, prediction and control in civil infrastructure O&M.',
    324: 'Addresses the micro-level gap of mapping live articulated-equipment motion into digital twins: orientation sensors (XSens MTw) on the boom, stick and bucket of a Caterpillar 430E IT backhoe drive forward-kinematic updates of a 3D twin with proximity monitoring, achieving a 0.06 m mean separation error with 0.05 m standard deviation in 15 configurations and testing audio-visual warnings against 2.0-3.0 m safety buffers.',
    329: 'Fills the granularity gap between abstract quality risk and concrete defects: a quality-defect-trigger concept with an evolution-mechanism, ontology-based four-layer semantic model and GraphDB linked-data pipeline uses SPARQL deviation computation to flag triggers exceeding tolerance thresholds, identifying a 4.63 mm x-axis misalignment and 2.9 mm seam-flatness deviation in a prefabricated composite-slab installation while reaching 100 percent identification accuracy in 371 s.',
    331: 'Provides an early conceptual bridge between BIM-based digital twinning and OHS decision-making: a scoping literature review plus a Research-through-Design proposal outlines a framework correlating safety management processes, project-level strategic decision-making, BIM-based digital twins and a Decision Support System to shift construction safety toward predictive analysis and all-worker inclusion.',
    332: 'Fills the gap between conceptual digital twins and on-site construction management: a Design Science Research study, grounded in the H2020 BIM2TWIN project, uses Living Lab questionnaires and interviews to rank on-site inefficiencies and digitalization barriers, then derives PDCA-classified user requirements and standardized BPMN workflows covering progress monitoring, quality control, health and safety, equipment control, and production planning.',
    333: 'Encodes the asset-twin coupled system as a dynamic decision network so data assimilation, uncertainty tracking, prediction, and maintenance planning share one framework: convolution-based deep learning classifies damage location and magnitude from vibration recordings (93.61 percent beam, 91.39 percent bridge accuracy), sequential Bayesian updates track health, and a health-dependent control policy recommends do-nothing, repair, or operation-restriction actions on synthetic cantilever-beam and Hornefors railway bridge cases.',
    334: 'Addresses the absence of modeling methodology for heritage corbelled dry-stone masonry: historical analysis of nuraghe construction techniques is linked to physical digital twins combining 3D surveys, historical documentation, and laboratory tests, with discrete block-based kinematics, friction, damage variables, and multiphysical weathering couplings, such as water diffusion, salt crystallisation, and thermal and chemical effects, framed through variational principles.',
    335: 'Bridges the GIS-territorial to BIM-building scale divide for multi-hazard assessment: the TERIMAAS framework centralizes BIM, GIS, and real-time IoT streams in a PostGIS repository that dynamically updates hazard, vulnerability, and risk scores, demonstrated on a flood risk case study of a public building in northwest Italy, giving stakeholders near real-time territorial and building-level risk views.',
    340: 'Demonstrates an operational UAV plus AMR inspection workflow synchronized with a cloud digital twin: a UAV with YOLOX detection, UPerNet segmentation, and LiDAR retro-reflectivity analysis covers vertical signage and vegetation, while an AMR measures horizontal markings, with MQTT and Node-RED data fusion into ontology-based KPI dashboards, validated at the A24 motorway Gran Sasso Nord site in central Italy, with sub-10-cm AMR navigation repeatability.',
    343: 'Fills the gap between image-only damage inspection and system-level planning: the graphics-based digital twin couples a SAP2000 finite element model with a photorealistic Blender computer graphics model of a 45-floor Guangzhou tower, validated against UAV photogrammetry point clouds, and uses earthquake damage hotspots plus environmental constraints to compare three UAV flight schemes, recommending a parallel path that stays within battery life.',
    347: 'Addresses the gap between robot teleoperation and safe collaborative construction: the I2PL-DT couples immersive VR with a ROS-connected KUKA arm so workers without programming skills perform high-level task planning, preview and approve collision-free motions, and supervise execution with bidirectional communication, verified on a drywall installation case with imperfect framing and a 20-subject human-in-the-loop study reporting positive usability.',
    349: 'Closes the missing loop between BIM and robotic construction: a Rhino-based BIM with layered shop-drawing data drives a KUKA KR120 robot through ROS and MoveIt, automatically generated Unity digital twins let humans approve plans and intervene, robot-proposed adaptations resolve parent and nearby-object deviations, and sensed as-built data are written back to the BIM, verified on a drywall installation case and block pick-and-place tests with 100 percent success at 10 mm gaps.',
    354: 'Synthesizes digital twin applications for prefabricated construction into a structured framework: the review identifies critical physical-digital integration points and proposes a digital twin framework spanning hoisting management, safety monitoring, and predictive analytics, organizing data acquisition, multi-source data modeling, and an intelligent construction platform with virtual agents coordinated through web-service-based service architecture.',
    357: 'Delivers hazard warnings through ambient vision rather than the occupied focal channel: YOLOv4-tiny with Deep SORT tracks objects from CCTV streams, a 4D BIM-based virtual construction site computes red, yellow, and blue danger zones, and Microsoft HoloLens 2 overlays them in real time, tested in three quasi-on-site scenarios with detection accuracy above 96.1 percent, a 72 square meter effective area, and 11.47 cm average alignment error.',
    358: 'Closes the gap between data-driven TFS models and operational control by embedding a BO-GCN-BiLSTM predictor and SHAP interpretation in a digital twin platform with bidirectional IoT and 5G links: on the Wuhan Metro Line 12 Yangtze tunnel it predicts slurry pressure across six geological types with average R-squared 0.935 and RMSE 0.162, outperforming six baselines, and iteratively keeps slurry pressure within the warning range.',
    359: 'Combines prediction and optimization for large-diameter slurry shield attitude: Bayesian-optimized CatBoost maps 19 construction parameters to six attitude targets with R-squared above 0.9 on three soils of the Yangtze River tunnel in Wuhan, SHAP finds push-group thrust dominant, and MOEAD multiobjective optimization improves attitude by up to 23.436 percent across five scenarios, embedded in a digital twin framework with warnings and parameter recommendations.',
    360: 'Fills the gap of fragmented tunnel surveillance video, separation of video and business data, and missing two- and three-dimensional linkage in tunnel digital operations: a BIM static scene model fused in real time with multi-channel surveillance video through 3D registration and projection plus multi-source IoT sensing data, demonstrated on a tunnel in China for traffic flow, accident rescue, facility management, and emergency response.',
    361: 'Addresses video fragmentation, subsystem data separation (AIS, smart bayonet) and untimely emergency response in inland waterway safety monitoring: drone tilt photography plus BIM build a static scene, multi-channel video is 3D-registered and fused with 25 cameras, and multi-source IoT data form a digital twin demonstrated on a Changhu-Shen Line segment with two- and three-dimensional linkage.',
    366: 'Bridges the gap between sparse on-site sensor readings and comprehensive understanding of building fire dynamics: an AIoT-integrated digital twin with LoRa wireless thermometry whose ADLSTM-Fire model reconstructs the full spatiotemporal temperature field from discrete sensor-array data (R2 93%) and forecasts fire development 60 s ahead (R2 92%), validated against CFD benchmarks and full-scale building fire experiments.',
    368: 'Fills the gap of edge-cloud collaborative intelligence for vibration anomaly detection and localization in high-rise buildings: a wireless time-synchronized smart sensor with LoRa chain synchronization below 20 microseconds and edge STFT anomaly detection, plus a cloud MDOF flexural-shear digital twin updated by SSI-COV and PSO that localizes sources via spectrum amplitude feature matching, validated on a 17-story building under 82.9 N shaking-table excitation.',
    372: 'Addresses the lack of spatial linkage between internal BIM components and external building scenes for structural health monitoring: IFC BIM is split into sub-BIMs and fused with an oblique-photogrammetry real-scene 3D Tiles model through rigid-body SVD registration and JSON semantic mapping, integrating 60 vibration, displacement, strain, and temperature sensors of the Nanjing Museum Old Hall into a Cesium-based monitoring system.',
    376: 'Fills the gap of three-dimensional near-miss detection at construction sites: drone imagery builds a BIM-based static scene and binocular cameras feed YOLOv5 target recognition, DeepSORT tracking, and SGM stereo matching into an Unreal Engine digital twin with protective envelopes and early warnings, detecting 1181 of 1300 near-misses (93.80% precision, 96.64% recall) in a one-month Foshan steel-hoisting pilot.',
    377: 'Extends near-miss management from 2D detection to in-process 3D prediction: YOLOv5, SGBM, DeepSORT and MediaPipe keypoints feed a non-autoregressive transformer that forecasts worker trajectories (ADE 0.134) and postures (ADE 0.501), reconstructed by an LBFGS inverse-kinematics solver in Unreal Engine, predicting near-misses with 93.32% precision and 96.08% recall across forklift, floor-opening, and material-lifting zones.',
    379: 'Moves shield tunneling digital twins from monitoring toward closed-loop decision support: a four-layer DT framework where SHAP identifies 16 key tunneling parameters and an ABC-NSGA-III hybrid optimizer solves six attitude objectives, achieving a 32.02% overall optimization rate and 2.21 to 17.13% attitude-deviation reduction on 100 rings of the Shanghai Airport Link Line, with optimized parameters fed back to guide operations.',
    382: 'Addresses the gap between static periodic inspections and real-time infrastructure maintenance: a LOD 400 BIM model of a solar-powered noise barrier tunnel integrated with the Wansan Tunnel in Jeonju is synchronized through Autodesk Forge API and WebSockets with vibration, tilt, light, air quality, and water detection sensors, achieving over 90% light-sensor transmission and detecting illuminance and structural anomalies during a 17-day demonstration.',
    386: 'Fills the gap of multi-source information transmission and DT-based early warning in deep-buried tunnel construction: multifunctional wireless base stations collect harmful gas, meteorological, deformation, and personnel-positioning data, mirrored in an OpenGL virtual tunnel with a four-level warning and emergency response mechanism, which successfully predicted a collapse at the K0+668 face of the 11.7 km Dongtianshan Tunnel with no casualties.',
    388: 'Overcomes the conflict between smoothness priors and sharp leakage boundaries in ERT dam monitoring: a topology-guided Fourier neural operator with decoupled geometric parameterization and a Navigator warm start localizes dam leakage with 99.7% success and 89.3% high-fidelity rates, accelerating forward modeling 345-fold and inversion 72-fold versus finite element methods, while remaining stable under 20% noise and 50% data loss.',
    389: 'Fills the gap of accurate real-time environment perception for bulldozer teleoperation in hazardous mine dumping: an anterior-time digital twin from UAV tilt photography achieves 0.6 cm average 3D error over 35,000 square meters, deep-learning retaining-wall edge detection reaches 0.923 precision and 0.877 F1, and a real-time platform with force, sound, and naked-eye 3D feedback supports a Shantui SD90 bulldozer, raising effective working time by 25%.',
    396: 'Fills the gap of an automated geometric digital twin method for cable dome structures: DS-gDT detects joints from point cloud data using a three-point normal cylinder fitting model with radius-constrained sampling and double termination criterion, then rebuilds topology via an adjacency matrix, achieving recognition about 51.5 percent above conventional RANSAC, 20.09 percent efficiency gain and above 99 percent joint-coordinate accuracy on a scaled dome.',
    398: 'Fills the gap between passive crane monitoring and proactive climbing-process safety control: the SINP framework couples process-based risk identification for the eight-step climbing cycle with GDTA-derived information requirements, then delivers navigation and alarms through IoT sensors and an edge intelligent control device, cutting dialogue counts from 11.8-12.2 to 0.8-1.6, completion times from 515.6-676.0 to 375.0-444.2 seconds and operational errors to zero in tests.',
    401: 'Fills the gap of precise 2D-to-3D defect localization with semantic enrichment: a GeoBIM-assisted digital twin registers UAV-detected facade defects onto georeferenced BIM models through SfM pose correction and virtual camera depth rendering, achieving centimeter-level accuracy (mean errors 0.49-1.36 cm versus 1-3 meters for GPS-based methods) and over 80 percent mAP0.5 detection at 30 FPS on a Hong Kong high-rise, including curved and heritage facades.',
    402: 'Fills the gap of a framework jointly covering digital twins and BIM level-of-details for construction site management: four interacting components (BIM digital representation, IoT, data storage-integration-analytics, physical-environment interaction) are extended with LoD-Graphics and LoD-Information levels from approximate to verified across all site stages, and 31 questionnaires plus 10 expert interviews confirm support for monitoring, quality, efficiency and safety.',
    404: 'Fills the gap of closed-loop digital twin control for aerial building machine jacking, validated on a 1:25 scale model of a 380-meter Wuhan project: PPO reinforcement learning tunes PID parameters and a transfer-learned DNN-PID controller with deviation coupling runs on an STM32 platform, reducing mean synchronization error to 0.377 mm versus 3.485, 0.463 and 0.709 mm for competing methods, staying below 0.46 mm across ten loading conditions with a 29 percent gain from transfer learning.',
    405: 'Fills the gap of system-level design methods for bridge construction digital twins: MBSE with a V-model architecture over the RFLP process models requirements, functions, logic and physics in SysML for monitoring a 90+90 meter cable-stayed bridge rotation (21,200 tons, 79 degrees), and a 1:100 scale prototype with DHT11, MPU6050, wind and laser displacement sensors over MQTT to Unreal Engine verifies data flow and threshold alarms.',
    408: 'Fills the gap between pixel-level defect recognition and physical severity quantification: CUBIT-InSeg provides 6996 high-resolution 4800x3200 UAV facade images with 62,187 crack and spalling instances, benchmarks over 80 models and zero-shot transfer on two cross-domain datasets, then converts masks into crack width, length and spalling area registered onto a digital twin with centimetre-level accuracy, graded per BS ISO 15686-7:2017 on a Hong Kong logistics building.',
    412: 'Fills the gap of a closed perception-analysis-decision-execution loop for human-robot collision warning: a five-dimensional digital twin fuses RGB-D and IMU data with Faster R-CNN, YOLOv5 and HRNet detection, achieving millimetre-level excavator key point deviations and over 96 percent dangerous-zone and 95 percent warning-zone prediction precision with about 0.13 second warning delay in a case study.',
    413: 'Fills the gap between theoretical process simulation and on-site tunnel management: a four-layer digital twin couples an AnyLogic discrete event simulation with Markov random field stochastic geology and AHP-DEMATEL vulnerability evaluation, and 2500 Monte Carlo runs on a real NATM tunnel estimate a 78.4 percent probability of finishing within the 1794-day plan, with the average estimated schedule differing from actual by only 9 days (0.50 percent).',
    414: 'Fills the gap of monitoring bridges that lack sensors by extending a digital twin across a regional bridge group: WIM data from six million vehicles is fitted with Gaussian mixtures and MCMC sampling to drive finite element models of three Jiangsu bridges, and Transformer encoder-decoder models predict responses with R2 above 0.99 (0.9970-0.9999), outperforming LSTM, BiLSTM and BiGRU and validated by field vehicle tests.',
    416: 'Fills the gap of static risk assessment that cannot track dynamic tunnel construction: a digital twin theory fuses IoT-collected data into geometry, physics and knowledge models (BIM, Midas, LSTM) with black-box, gray-box and white-box accuracy levels, and LSTM prediction of vault settlement (RMSE 0.0929 mm, maximum error about 0.135 mm) drives displacement-level safety grading against a 120 mm design limit.',
    418: 'Fills the gap between out-of-sync site investigation and simulation in collapse forensics: a digital twin built from BIM, finite element and physics engine models reconstructs the multistage life cycle of a seven-story hotel retrofitted from a four-story steel frame, reproduces the collapse and matches simulated wreckage with actual debris, showing welding-induced column buckling and plastic deformation caused the failure rather than local buckling alone.',
    420: 'Combines DT technology with prefabricated BIM to model prefabricated building construction, so measuring sensors monitor displacement and rotation torque during component production, transport, and assembly, and risk indicators are tracked in real time. Validation uses factor analysis on risk cases (130 valid cases, 100 percent effective, extraction values 0.75 to 0.86), filling the gap of few DT studies on prefabricated construction in smart cities.',
    421: 'Establishes a correlation mechanism between structural design parameters and mechanical parameters and fuses it with a four-level geometry-physics-behavior-rule digital twin, training a BP neural network on finite element samples to intelligently predict construction safety of a string beam. Predicted vertical displacement and lower-chord cable stress were verified against field measurements, providing a basis for safety control.',
    423: 'Extends the IFC schema with IfcDSMSystem, IfcMonitoringItem, and IfcSensorAssembly entities to integrate dam safety monitoring information into a dam digital twin, then automates continuous safety evaluation with multi-rule cloud reasoning, a multi-dimensional cloud model, and an improved CRITIC weighting method, demonstrated on the 131 m Jiangya gravity dam from January to September 2019.',
    426: 'Proposes a five-layer digital twin framework for building machine jacking operations, creating parametric twin models in Blender geometric node groups (98.48 percent auto-generation accuracy) and an RBF neural network for online stress and deformation prediction with relative errors within 0.1 percent and 6 percent respectively, verified on a 186.3 m Wuhan building where five major accidents were avoided and jacking efficiency rose 19.75 percent.',
    427: 'Builds a whole-lifecycle construction process optimization framework integrating a data management system, BIM modelling system, and Flexsim digital twin across survey, design, construction, and operation phases, feeding detected problems back to the BIM model to eliminate information islands. A BP neural network diagnoses eight construction fault types with 99 percent average accuracy versus 90.23, 89.19, and 88.35 percent for CNN, SVM, and PSO baselines.',
    428: 'Equips an excavator with four IMU sensors and two GNSS receivers, estimates its 3D pose via an Euler-based kinematic model refined by social spider algorithm optimization, cutting bucket tip mean error from 64.59 mm to 24.61 mm, and couples it with a BIM of buried pipes in Unity for real-time collision risk assessment with 30 cm and 50 cm warning zones, applied to a 1760 m Shandong pipe project.',
    429: 'Integrates TBM excavation data into a BIM as-built model through a Dynamo computational design algorithm on a 2.4 km French tunnelling project, automatically placing segments from corrected TPC and VMT positioning, embedding segment manufacturing traceability and no-drill zones, and cutting ring modelling time from 15 to 20 minutes to 1 minute, a cycle time reduction above 90 percent supporting bracketry design and clash detection.',
}

AI = {
    6: 'Deployment lessons rather than controlled validation: one real work zone, and the predictive framework (conflict metrics, C-V2X warnings) stays at framework level without demonstrated closed-loop actuation; no explicit future work is stated.',
    7: 'Purely conceptual: none of the scenarios is implemented or validated, and the paper itself lists open challenges of a missing information model for DTs, missing version management guidelines, missing communication latency guidelines, and missing interoperability standards analogous to IFC.',
    13: 'Conceptual only: the framework was validated through a thematic analysis of 37 studies and a survey of FM professionals (66 responses, 28 complete) rather than a live implementation; no prototype or sensor deployment is reported. Future work includes a Delphi study with a broader panel and involving firefighters as end users.',
    14: 'No actuation or bidirectional link to building systems: forecasting models are offline-trained and never updated online. The platform relies on proprietary ArcGIS, assumes a reliable wireless network, and sensor accuracy under extreme conditions is unverified; future work targets open-source visualization and integration with more real assets for active response and evacuation mechanisms.',
    19: 'The two DT cases are management and visualization platforms lacking AI or simulation protocols, which the authors state are still under research, and the paper proposes definitions rather than new empirical validation; the European standard was still pending publication and no quantitative evaluation is offered.',
    20: 'Smart Twins 4.0 is limited to a single physical resource (formwork), has restricted data analysis capabilities and interoperability, and still requires manual steps in data collection; the model simplifies real-world complexity, omits human roles beyond decision-making, and the authors state it needs future testing in different contexts.',
    21: 'No automated defect detection: annotations are manually created by human inspectors, which the authors call the main bottleneck for scaling; validation covers only two UAV datasets, hyperparameters are not systematically optimized, and the system assumes reliable connectivity. Future work includes automated detection, temporal change monitoring, 3D Gaussian Splatting visualization, and offline capabilities.',
    22: 'Detection is anomaly-based rather than damage localization or quantification, which the authors list as future work; validation is limited to one short-span bridge pilot, and analytics still rely on middleware plus cloud, with plans to move FFT and inference onto energy-harvesting edge sensors and to extend to wind towers and broader production deployments.',
    23: 'No sensors are yet deployed: the study covers only Building Virtualization and part of sensor data analysis, so the EWS and DT feedback loop remain pending; validation relies on historical damage reports and analytical consistency, with future research to include experimental models, tri-axial sensor installation, and ambient-vibration calibration of the numerical model.',
    35: 'Entirely conceptual: no implementation, prototype, or case evaluation is presented, so none of the requirements or tools is tested. The authors list open challenges of integrating uncertain data sources and heterogeneous models, evaluating intelligent tools for the resilience cycle, and IT scalability and reliability, proposing federated digital twins instead of monolithic implementations.',
    42: 'A short conference-stage contribution: only parameter identification on a numerical shear beam example is demonstrated, with no deployed structure, no live sensor data, and no quantitative surrogate accuracy reported; the conclusion and future work sections remain essentially undeveloped, so the real-time SHM surrogate role is proposed rather than validated.',
    44: 'One-way digital shadow: the dashboard informs managers but does not control site operations, technology readiness did not permit acting weekly on extracted insights, and feedback came only after development. Bottlenecks include logistics, privacy, need for specialized crews, sensor fragility, and manual progress updates; automating data collection and treatment is future work.',
    45: 'Monitoring is campaign-based rather than live: the twin is an offline validated finite-element model with no continuous data link or actuation, higher-order modes are missed at the 100 Hz sampling rate, and the six-phase Incident Response Framework is proposed but not yet deployed; higher-rate testing is noted for the future.',
    46: 'Offline, camera-based pipeline with manual image capture and fiducial marker attachment; 2D segmentation precision averages only 50.4 percent, small-diameter rebar inspection reaches only 77.8 percent, and registration fails on geometrically indistinct structures; future work points to more training data, augmentation, unsupervised techniques and Point Transformer based classification.',
    47: 'Validation rests on a scaled laboratory testbed with simplified boundary conditions, not field monitoring; time-dependent processes like consolidation and creep are ignored, settlement and lining deformation are modeled separately, and no real-time sensor link exists; future work targets field monitoring data, spatio-temporal Transformers, layered soil and groundwater, coupled models and continuous model updating.',
    49: 'Data quality dependency is acknowledged: sensor noise, loss, calibration drift and delays can misclassify risk levels; the ontology and rules are manually built for Shanghai urban tunnels, limiting scalability; reasoning speed, throughput and prediction accuracy are not quantitatively benchmarked; single-project validation; future work includes confidence metrics, automated rule generation, dynamic learning and stress testing.',
    50: 'The available record states no explicit future work; validation is documented only for the mobile gin pole application, and whether the TROA-ET surrogate is updated online, transferred to other equipment types, or tested against field disturbances beyond the stated scenario is not established.',
    61: 'One-way implementation: digital models are loaded with measured traffic loads but no feedback or control channel back to physical bridges exists, and deriving bridge health status from simulation results to form more interaction tasks between the two spaces is left as future exploration.',
    65: 'Results come from simulated emergency scenarios, and continuous TCP/IP connectivity is assumed, so deep subterranean network degradation could break the fog-to-mobile pipeline; speech recognition reaches only a 14.2 percent word error rate under 85 dB noise, and the app runs only on Android and Linux; future plans include signaling and control integration to automatically stop trains and escalators.',
    66: 'Expert-driven and weakly operationalized: only nine Delphi experts limit objectivity, results are tied to one specific project, and the model remains at a development stage with unquantified technical and methodological challenges; future research targets higher applicability and accuracy, larger samples across project types, and artificial intelligence and big data integration.',
    67: 'Purely conceptual: the framework is built only on literature analysis and existing tools, has not been validated in any real-world scenario, and needs ongoing updates to track technology; future research should run pilot implementations and case studies across regions, disaster types and bridge systems, and improve technology integration and data management.',
    68: 'Validated only in simulation: Gazebo idealizes robot-human collaboration and material handling, human worker actions are not modeled, and the LLM is limited to constraint extraction; extending to further construction scenarios, proactive conflict detection and pre-optimization reasoning are future work, with physical robot deployment still pending.',
    72: 'Proof-of-concept scope: a single renovation project, functional verification only, no quantified cost, schedule or safety improvements, a short evaluation period, a TAM sample biased to early-career professionals, manual data entry, and no AI or predictive analytics beyond historical KPI visualization; future work calls for multi-site validation, longitudinal studies, IoT automation, deep-learning prediction and cognitive twin capabilities.',
    74: 'Conceptual only, with no implementation or validation; the framework is a recommendation that still awaits application, and the authors state it must be proven through multiple case studies with diverse asset uses and complexities, recommending energy efficiency and indoor environmental quality as neglected test fields.',
    76: 'The prototypes are proof of concept: only a small subset of live sensor data was explored, no analytics or prediction were incorporated, asset placement was manual with positional errors up to 1 metre, and no formal usability tests were run. Future work includes automated progress quantification, live worker tracking with wearables, analytics, data security and Datasmith scalability trials.',
    78: 'No live site data link; the model is a static simulation whose parameters come from a limited questionnaire sample, and its reliability and predictive capability are acknowledged as weaker than data-driven methods. Authors propose larger samples, EEG and eye-tracking for psychophysiological data, and adding agent-to-agent interactions as future work.',
    84: 'Scan-to-BIM remains semi-automated and the DT provides no automatic defect detection; updates come in batch from inspections rather than a real-time link. Future work covers a method to integrate inspection and monitoring results into DTs, extension to new bridges during design, and linking DTs into networks for whole transport corridors.',
    86: 'Validation is numerical, using a 48 m steel roof structural model with five working conditions rather than a monitored real project; the paper reports no live site data or actuation and no explicit limitations section. Future direction stated is only to deepen digital twin research for construction safety assessment and structural optimization design.',
    88: 'Defect information modeling relies on custom JSON files that lack extensibility, and the multi-module stack risks cross-platform compatibility issues as functionality grows. Future work targets redefining defect and damage data in IFC format, improving cross-platform interoperability and scalability for more advanced bridge DT applications.',
    92: 'The framework has not yet been validated with field or laboratory tests, and its large Bayesian network demands 97,484.8 MB of memory just to store conditional probability tables, limiting practical scale-up. Future work includes custom Bayesian networks to cut computation, validation through field coring and lab testing, and adding restoration and resilience modelling.',
    97: 'Only robot-operator collision risk is detected automatically; tracking of other workspace elements must still be added, and the system awaits calibration of assembly tools and tests with real carpenters. Future work includes defining shared human-robot spaces, optimizing auxiliary trajectories and tool orientations, and handling robot payload constraints.',
    100: 'No new data were created or analyzed in the study; the framework builds on prior experiments and model stages, and the digital twin stage remains offline without a live monitoring link. No explicit future work is stated, leaving integration into operator maintenance planning and validation on instrumented structures open.',
    102: 'Results come entirely from simulation of a 20.4 by 20.1 metre floor with 80 to 160 people; the system is not deployed with real sensors or a live building, and no quantitative accuracy beyond simulated evacuation times is reported. Future work extends to more complex layouts, wheelchair users and falling evacuees.',
    104: 'High-resolution perception and large-model inference raise computational and maintenance costs, edge computing depends on stable power and network, AR execution relies on worker adaptation, and validation covers a single SCP project with confidential raw data. Future research targets model compression, lightweight deployment and adaptive zoning for scalability.',
    106: 'The system is limited to integrating and visually presenting multi-source data; heterogeneous format standardization between BIM and point clouds remains a major challenge, and prediction or assessment is absent. Future research will add advanced data analytics and machine learning to predict maintenance needs and potential problems from historical and real-time data.',
    109: 'Geospatial information alone cannot support full risk-informed decisions, localization still relies on smartphone sensors without ranging instruments, and participation depends on citizens willingness to contribute data. Future work includes integrating textual, audio and IoT sources, incentive mechanisms for participation, and more case studies to evaluate spatiotemporal updating.',
    110: 'The pilot covers only water supply and gas pipelines, lacking power and communication monitoring modules, and its data is not yet connected to Pudong Airport systems for cross-node emergency linkage; multi-type pipeline adaptability and cross-departmental data interface standards are stated as future work.',
    111: 'The system relies on a single UAV constrained by battery endurance, and its detector drops to 41.5 to 47.1 percent mAP50 on public UAV datasets, so generalization remains limited; future work includes multi-UAV cooperation, resilience in adverse weather and low light, extra sensors such as infrared and LiDAR, and broader training datasets.',
    112: 'PosTraFormer has the largest parameter count (5661.7K) and lowest speed (288.8 frames per second) among tested models, and training relies on simulated trajectories because stacking datasets are scarce, with only 70 real pose sets for fine-tuning; no explicit future work is stated, so data collection and lightweight deployment remain unaddressed.',
    115: 'Validation is confined to a laboratory analogue of a stationary tower crane, so no quantitative on-site performance could be measured, and the MPU-6050 readings were excluded from the twin because of latency and twitching; the authors propose a proprietary MCU package and dedicated connections instead of open Wi-Fi as future work.',
    118: 'The closed-loop digital twin workflow remains a design proposal rather than a deployed system, and the field validation used simplified inputs: uniform friction angle of 32 degrees, tensile strength of 17 MPa, Kirsch-based stress and a kinematic-only weighting; the authors plan spatio-temporal point process and Bayesian hierarchical models for clustered failures.',
    121: 'The monitoring platform currently covers only the foundation pit construction stage, and the app runs only on Android with compatibility still needing improvement; sensor stability differences make the multi-source fusion platform costly and time-consuming, and no explicit future work section is provided beyond these stated gaps.',
    122: 'Experiments lasted a limited period in a controlled staging area, RTK-GNSS suffers signal loss and interference, and operator awareness of workers could not be recorded, so head-pose or eye-tracking data is proposed; future work includes longer data collection, other equipment types, drone-based condition capture, big data analytics and standards for safe distances.',
    125: 'The assessment depends entirely on expert questionnaires (20 for indicator weighting, 15 valid in the case study), so results are subjective despite probability-based aggregation, and one ACS case limits generalizability; the authors propose update-frequency thresholds, sensor log data to replace expert judgment, and extension to other sectors.',
    128: 'The strain interpolation requires predefined mathematical representations and fails for live loads with moving locations; only tensile strain is monitored, not shear or torsion, and validation used a small-scale frame in a controlled environment, so the authors will run full-scale laboratory and field tests with additional sensors.',
    129: 'Sensing equipment is exposed to humidity, dust and vibration, so measurements can drift and regular calibration is required, and future validation will quantify mean-time-to-failure and accuracy decline in real tunnel conditions; the authors also plan to optimize the fusion and prediction algorithms and extend the system to mine tunneling and urban underground space.',
    137: 'Accuracy was not compared with field survey data, which the authors admit is needed to evaluate the method, and only underpass roads are handled; future research will validate through field surveys, focus groups and expert interviews, and extend the approach to overpasses, bridges, tunnels and traffic safety facilities.',
    138: 'The system is only applied to one station project, sensor equipment still needs anticorrosion and anti-interference development, and the numerical analysis model must be improved for true two-way mapping between digital and physical worlds; future work includes prediction algorithms, web, GIS, 5G and blockchain integration for multi-station unified management.',
    141: 'Only verified by fire accident simulation; on-site experiments are still needed. The approach assumes IoT terminal data are fully obtainable and well processed, and only three basic fire protection scenarios are investigated. Future work covers a unified hardware-software platform for validation, more fire protection scenarios refined by domain experts, and extension to other system control tasks such as active seismic response control.',
    143: 'Results come from a laboratory scale model under simplified single-behavior conditions; sensor data agree with the virtual model in trend but differ in magnitude due to material property differences. Combined environmental loads and other unsafe behaviors, tower crane structural changes, and component influence weights during instability remain future work, and the unsafe hoisting monitoring system is only planned, not built.',
    144: 'Validated only on a scaled-down crane in the laboratory, neglecting dynamic site environments and operator-specific habits; mapping suffers cumulative errors, and events like untested lifting and reverse operation show low accuracy or elevated false alarms requiring manual verification. Future work: analyzing consistency disparity sources, developing a more comprehensive mapping framework, and collecting real-world hoisting data.',
    148: 'No live site data link: IoT sensor collection, user interfaces, and on-site usability are explicitly out of scope, and the framework is tested only on one high-rise case study. Query translation remains too technical for practitioners, and scalability bottlenecks are expected on larger graphs. Future work adds schedule dependencies, compliance results, real-time location tracking, LLM-based query generation, and game-engine dissemination.',
    154: 'Case studies are static snapshots of two jobsites without live data integration. Segmentation is expected to degrade in rain, fog, or dim light and under occlusions and moving objects; volumetric measurement overestimates unstacked piles because RGB cameras cannot see inside them. Building robust machine vision accounting for these challenges is the direction of ongoing research.',
    155: 'Relies on static Google Street View and UAV imagery with no live wind or site monitoring; facade occlusion by cars and trees degrades window detection, and performance drops in rain and fog. HAZUS assumptions such as uniform gravel size and persistent wind direction and the lack of validation against real disaster cases remain; collecting such data at scale is future work.',
    158: 'The UUT model is a one-time static LiDAR scan with no live facility data link, and the four-degree-of-freedom platform cannot support yaw or sway motions required by diverse VR applications; cybersickness symptoms still vary by age, and only 17 participants were tested. Extending the platform toward five degrees of freedom with a rotary drive for 360-degree yaw is underway.',
    163: 'Monitoring only with no actuation or closed control of building systems. Validation is limited to the use phase, with no case studies from other lifecycle phases, and no quantitative comparison of detection speed and accuracy against conventional fire detection methods. Cost, lack of adoption knowledge, and manual 3D model generation remain obstacles; these comparisons and lifecycle studies are future research.',
    165: 'Validated only on a small laboratory-scale 3D-printed pipe, with verification against the finite element model rather than in-service plant data; sensor noise, measurement uncertainty, and scale effects are not addressed, and no explicit future work is stated beyond the expectation that continuous development will transfer the system to ports, shipbuilding, power generation, and manufacturing.',
    167: 'The geometric virtual model is not synchronized between UAV image updates, so same-day erected structures and moving equipment are missed; surface temperature simulation overestimates by up to 23.6 C for asphalt, and manual material registration is labor-intensive. UAV infrared thermography is computationally demanding at site scale. Future research targets integrating biometric sensors for individualized worker heat risk assessment.',
    168: 'Validated through simulation only, with no real fire deployment. Risk assessment considers just three fire risk factors and assumes average walking speed, ignoring obstacles, blocked paths, age, and disability; recognition accuracy depends on the completeness of the knowledge base, and computing and network resources may be strained as buildings and sensors scale. Future work covers generative-AI scenario generation and personalized risk assessment.',
    176: 'Restricted to the linear elastic stage of materials, excluding plasticity, nonlinear behavior, and multiphysics coupling, and validated only on a laboratory crane boom; prediction accuracy depends on the limited high-fidelity sample set, and sensor uncertainty is modeled but not eliminated. Future work should explore nonlinear materials, plastic deformation, and multiphysics coupling for a more realistic twin.',
    178: 'The full methodology is not yet demonstrated end to end on a real damaged building; BIM geometry is simplified and alignment errors distort labels near beam-column connections, 3D change detection misses light damage, and no structural analysis is yet integrated. Future work includes physics-based graphics model validation and coupling damage states to pre-earthquake analysis to predict global safety.',
    181: 'Stage C defect detection is not implemented; segmentation still confuses leadwork and other classes, generalization drops sharply on unseen buildings, and occlusions such as chimneys can survive the median merging as shadows. Future work covers more roof data, SAM-based segmentation, defect detection in the semantic segments, and populating and maintaining the roof digital logbook.',
    183: 'Validation is limited to laboratory plexiglass pipe segments rather than in-service networks; the method cannot measure the underwater part of pipes and does not suit bends with curved axes. Future work includes fusing 3D sonar data, AI-based assessment of spalling, corrosion and open joints, and an in-pipe inspection robot to carry the laser scanner.',
    185: 'Models are trained offline on historical data without stated online updating, only torsional vibration is validated as a fault type, and warning thresholds rely on statistical residuals rather than any closed-loop actuation of the dredger. Follow-up work should investigate internal relations and interaction mechanisms among different types of mechanical faults.',
    194: 'The IFC model carries only geometric data, connecting members are simplified as rectangular prisms without internal detail, and the FEM assumes zero displacement at the cable anchorage. Future work includes supplementing material, load and construction information in the IFC data and adjusting boundary stiffness based on monitoring data.',
    195: 'Validation covers one mobile manipulator prototype in controlled scenarios with protective equipment and human supervision, and virtual-state updates still depend on robot actuators for stopping. Future work targets more robot types including humanoids, faster perception methods with less latency, and predictive motion models to improve protective separation distance calculation.',
    196: 'Validation used only three sensor locations in one Taipei garage with simulated gas, standard-gas calibration is recommended for quantitative readings, and battery capacity limits node operation to about one week. Future work includes adopting more IoT technologies and integrating BIM with AI for smarter environment management in smart cities.',
    203: 'The training sample set is very limited (three integrated time points, expert-copied and expanded) and no intelligent decision system or automatic actuation exists; integration with hoisting risk assessment and prediction methods remains open. Future research will expand data samples to improve accuracy and enhance the BIM platform visualization and functional modules.',
    204: 'Validation data samples are acknowledged as insufficient, the mined rules lack an intelligent evaluation system, and single-project results cannot transfer to other projects without recalibration; no automated control loop is implemented. Future work integrates this coupling method with other prefabricated hoisting safety twin services.',
    205: 'The system is demonstrated only on a 1:10 scale test model rather than a full-scale project, and the authors acknowledge intelligent tensioning research is still preliminary with the DBN trained on historical mining data. Further work calls for deeper digital twin and AI integration and improved information collection and communication for whole-process tensioning control.',
    207: 'The model outputs single data points of peak cable force and displacement, not time-history responses, and is trained offline without online updating; 5G real-time transmission stability for large structures is an open challenge. Future research covers big data technologies for O and M data and integration with health monitoring and maintenance policy services.',
    208: 'The SVM models are trained offline on 15 days of simulated danger data from one stairwell room, danger coefficient scoring depends on safety staff judgment, and danger handling still falls to human staff. Future work targets more targeted handling suggestions, additional dangers such as harmful gas leaks, and extending digital twin models to structural and equipment safety management.',
    210: 'The training set uses real site monitoring values with error superposition, the model is offline-trained on one project with only four days of jacking data, and no automated warning integration exists; the authors plan multi-source sensor fusion with real-time monitoring systems and evaluation of generalization across different steel structures and construction conditions.',
    211: 'The random forest provides importance ranking rather than prediction accuracy metrics, safety control relies on rule-based alarms and shutdown commands without learning-based updating, and only one airport project validates the method; the authors state data transmission efficiency must improve and plan extension to bridges and high-rise platforms with better sensors and optimized predictive algorithms.',
    219: 'Data flow is not real-time but manual and intermittent, assets are uniform with no deterioration models, and there is no traffic crash or fuel consumption simulation; the tornado scenario is demonstrative rather than validated, and the authors list future work on mods for real-time data flow, deterioration tracking and empirical validation.',
    221: 'Only exposed drainage channels and topography are modeled, cross-sections use one uniform empirical size, the closure heuristic may wrongly connect distinct channels, and the twin is static with no live monitoring data; the authors plan real-time sensor integration, hydrodynamic simulation, data-driven susceptibility analysis and higher-LOD models toward fully realized digital twins.',
    225: 'The twin is an initial prototype with manual visual inspection input and no automated synchronization, initial post-construction inspection data were missing so the initial serviceability index could not be computed, and five-year single-point data produce wide eight-year intervention intervals; future work covers automating information input and model creation from point clouds and building performance databases.',
    226: 'The model is static with no real-time synchronization, digital inspection missed fine shrinkage cracks, portal overexposure prevents accurate color extraction, internet access is required for server connection, and point cloud density depends on scanning equipment; the authors plan additional information layers and UAV or ROV LiDAR acquisition for hard-to-reach tunnels.',
    235: 'No IoT sensors or live data feed the app yet, formats remain authoring-based rather than open standards, and no AI or ML processing exists, so the cognitive digital twin is aspirational; future work includes IoT networks, AI and AR/VR integration, whole-asset fire risk mapping and active wayfinding for evacuation.',
    238: 'Validation is testbed-only with two datasets, energy consumption was not instrumented, one-shot HPO is sensitive to concept drift, and open adversarial environments are not covered; the authors plan drift-triggered re-tuning, Metropolis-Hastings consensus for ring topologies, multi-objective accuracy-latency-energy optimization and Byzantine-robust aggregation.',
    239: 'Experiments run in a controlled testbed with emulated sensors rather than an active construction site, the digital twin supports monitoring and control commands but no autonomous actuation, and only general safety prediction is covered; the authors plan field deployment, additional data features, accident-specific models and fairness plus long-term robustness evaluation.',
    247: 'Operational energy penalties are conceptually inferred rather than dynamically simulated, embodied carbon uses ICE v3.0 proxy factors without Nigerian EPDs, records span only five years, and the digital twin is a conceptual prototype not validated for operational control; the authors plan Nigerian EPDs, 15-20 year monitoring, climate-zone verification and gradual twin operationalization.',
    253: 'It is a literature review without its own ontology or case validation; findings are limited to building construction execution papers retrieved by April 2023 and exclude infrastructure projects; barriers include unpublished ontologies causing redundancy, scalability limits and mapping complexity, with future work on reuse best practices, IoT-linked real-time semantic data and scalable solutions.',
    254: 'Detection relies on RGB imagery so vegetation-hidden or subsurface defects are missed, lighting variation and UAV motion degrade robustness, siltation-B and collapse-B classes reach only 0.60 accuracy with signs of overfitting, and validation covers a single site without live sensing; the authors plan multispectral and thermal sensors, LiDAR and edge AI inference.',
    255: 'Validation is limited to TUM office interiors with a manually labelled dataset; detection is weaker for objects that vary across buildings and many classes like furniture remain missing; only simple geometric primitives are fitted, point-cloud registration stays manual, and the photogrammetric step needs enough overlapping images. Future work adds more classes, CAD-level shapes, and joint 2D and 3D deep learning.',
    262: 'The actuator and HVAC responses to threshold breaches are designed but not implemented, semantic ontology integration remains unexplored, and the pilot lacks construction progress tracking and complaint channels; low-cost sensor reliability and a calibration loop are open issues, while Forge visualization of large datasets caused performance bottlenecks. Future work targets cognitive DT components, semantic standards, AI analytics and complaint management.',
    265: 'The model is linear and ignores solar radiation and nonlinear constraint effects, so real displacements may be underestimated; satellite and weather data are processed offline with no live monitoring link, and findings need generalization to other bridges. The authors suggest integrating L-band radar, GNSS, TInSAR, optical fibre and LiDAR measurements.',
    271: 'Evaluation rests on only 30 samples of one fastener type, with no comparison against real LiDAR scans, no long-term field tests and no validation of downstream anomaly detection; accuracy depends on input image and depth quality, and uncertainty remains for other fastener types and environments. Future work includes MiDaS-based depth estimation, anomaly detection algorithms and additional data sources.',
    273: 'Validation covers a single mid-sized academic building and three scenarios, Wi-Fi localization error stays non-negligible, and occupant privacy plus data governance are unresolved; agent-level behavioural modelling and multi-building validation were beyond scope. Future work includes predictive hazard modelling, sensor fusion (BLE, IMU, UWB), privacy-preserving architectures and larger building typologies.',
    278: 'Analyses remain linear-elastic with soil parameters taken from literature and an assumed 30 MPa concrete strength due to missing data, so nonlinear joint behavior is uncharacterized; monitoring data cannot be shared, and no automated live BIM-FEM coupling exists yet. Future research targets automatic interoperability, nonlinear fracture modelling at joints, and early warning systems for other dams.',
    283: 'The work is purely conceptual with no implemented system, sensor deployment or case validation, and conclusions rely on a narrow set of studies and the authors individual project experience. The paper calls for future research on safeguarding shared data and information security, human-machine interface issues, psychological impacts of automation, regulatory compliance, and machine learning extensions.',
    292: 'The twin is a static information model without real-time IoT ingestion, bidirectional communication or automated updates, relying on periodic surveys and semi-automated processing with manual intervention; behavioral and performance indicators are absent and only one urban area was tested, with data governance and privacy unresolved. Future work covers sensor integration, deep learning automation and city-wide scaling.',
    297: 'All evidence comes from simulations and idealized models rather than a deployed sensor network, so real-time underground monitoring is asserted but not demonstrated; risk assessment uses assumed probabilities, and the authors note insufficient equipment and data collection delayed earlier intelligent planning. No explicit future work or limitations section is provided beyond these points.',
    298: 'Evaluation metrics are comparative estimates rather than measured outcomes, convergence station readings were collected manually on a weekly basis until obstructed, and reflective targets had to be replaced mid-project; real-time processing of large geotechnical datasets demands high-performance computing and validation covers only one geological setting. Future research targets enhanced automation, predictive analytics and wider environments.',
    299: 'Flood scenarios are simulated offline with static 6-hour inundation data, live traffic is not yet ingested in real time, and no feedback or alerting loop exists; analysis covered only two Houston zip-code zones, and the model neglects inundation duration, drainage mitigation and non-flood traffic disruptions, with MSE rising after the twelfth interval. Future work targets automated real-time pipelines and broader geographic validation.',
    300: 'The dataset covers a single building case, processing still requires manual intervention rather than an end-to-end automated loop, and detection is limited to thermal defects such as thermal bridges and insulation damage, with weak recognition of fine cracks, weathering or mold; field findings also included false alarms from air-conditioner units. Future research targets multi-climate benchmark datasets, multimodal fusion, cloud plus 5G automation and large language model maintenance agents.',
    302: 'Prediction results still differ from laboratory experiments because of numerical-simulation simplification and parameter uncertainty; validation covers one indoor DIC test and a single landslide, the surrogate learns from simulation rather than live sensor feedback, and the digital twin only visualizes and predicts without early-warning actuation or closed-loop control of the physical slope.',
    308: 'The adhesion mechanism cannot handle highly rough surfaces and only surface cracks and spalling are analyzed, leaving UWB radar and infrared subsurface data unused; validation is limited to laboratory specimens and one residential building, and future work targets robot hardware adaptation to complex facades plus subsurface defect characterization through multi-modal cross-validation.',
    309: 'The digital twin is an offline simulation-to-reality data generator rather than a live synchronized model; only planetary-wheel faults of the RV reducer are considered on a laboratory test rig, and online diagnosis, model updating, or integration with an operating construction robot is not demonstrated or stated as future work.',
    313: 'The tool supports planning rather than real-time emergency operations, with no live sensor feeds, no actuation, and validation limited to Vienna city center; the authors plan alignment with EU regulations including NIS2, integration of Copernicus real-time streams, downscaled or locally calibrated solar data, and extension to compound events such as power outages and floods.',
    315: 'Theoretical simulation results were not validated by thorough field tests, the case focuses mainly on main-girder stress, and warnings still require personnel to execute predefined procedures rather than automatic control; future work includes comparing the digital twin approach with conventional construction safety control and building a large-scale cable-stayed bridge construction monitoring database.',
    318: 'Decision factors cover only water content, lithology and integrity; GPR captures a single cross-section so longitudinal integrity variation is missing, databases are unevenly sized, and per-cycle computation of 10-60 s grows to 2-5 minutes for concurrent tunnels; the authors propose GPU and KD-tree acceleration plus extension to soft-soil and underwater tunnels.',
    320: 'The method depends on dense, costly sensor arrays; several displacements are still measured manually with inclinometers, soil is idealized as homogeneous and isotropic, and consolidation over time and groundwater seepage are ignored; future work targets real-time sensing with AI-driven risk prediction, better sensor placement, and seepage and time-dependent effects.',
    321: 'Validation is limited to the Hedong Bridge case with no reported quantitative accuracy for the detection and prediction models; real-time performance depends on multi-source data integration speed, machine-learning robustness depends on training data quality, and uncertain expert rules complicate knowledge base construction; future work includes advanced ML algorithms and automatic knowledge-base selection per bridge type.',
    322: 'Validation is qualitative and conceptual only, demonstrating operational feasibility and logical consistency without numerical performance tests or comparisons with other systems; formalizing context-dependent expert knowledge into computable rules remains unresolved, multi-source data systems are costly, and future work targets autonomous learning, cross-infrastructure knowledge transfer, and full-lifecycle risk management.',
    324: 'Validation used a stationary backhoe in an indoor facility with a flat virtual ground model, bucket geometric differences and 0.5-degree sensor accuracy causing discrepancies; safety-buffer penetration rose with operating speed (15 to 68 percent), so dynamic tolerance zones, linear encoders, operator training, and extension to cranes, dump trucks and graders are identified as future work.',
    329: 'The framework depends on high-quality real-time data, lacks a standardized defect-trigger grading and remediation system, offers limited BIM and mobile-platform integration and weak visualization, and management-related and human-related triggers remain under-detected; future work targets data robustness, multiplatform DT integration, grading models, and reinforcement learning or large language model support.',
    331: 'It is a preliminary conceptual framework with no prototype, sensor integration, live data link, or implementation; the authors concede many shortcomings in the initial version and call for in-depth strategic analysis, development of a functional model for the executive level of construction companies, and alignment with real construction project contingencies.',
    332: 'Remains a conceptual architecture with no implemented platform, live sensor link, or field validation; real-time data acquisition, AI-driven knowledge extraction, and closed-loop correction are described only as future scenarios. Authors propose multi-site BDT portfolios with a broker, a Digital Twin Federator across city-scale DTs, and KPIs feeding automated learning as future work.',
    333: 'Validated only on noise-corrupted synthetic data from reduced-order physics models, with no real sensing or field deployment; neural networks, transition dynamics, and the control policy are all learned offline, and the fixed transition models made bridge deterioration predictions too optimistic. Future work targets online learning of transition dynamics from past data and reinforcement-learning planning over a finite asset-life horizon.',
    334: 'Purely a review and methodology proposal: no digital twin has been constructed, no numerical experiments or validation are reported, and no live data connection is considered. Future challenges listed by the authors include progressively adding coupled multiphysical weathering phenomena one at a time and building calibrated models of specific nuraghe structures.',
    335: 'Demonstrates only flood risk on one public building, so transfer to other hazards and regions is unproven; the approach needs substantial data infrastructure and expertise, and the centralized repository raises privacy, security, and single-point-of-failure concerns. Future work includes decentralized storage, multi-hazard modules, open-source BIM tooling, and AI-based extreme-event forecasting.',
    340: 'Validated only in clear daylight conditions, with sensor accuracy unproven in rain, fog, or low light and the Jetson Orin GPU running near capacity, limiting model complexity; EU regulation 2022/1426 currently bars fully autonomous AMR operation on open roads, and the twin only reports conditions without actuation. Future work covers sensor redundancy, adverse-weather training, predictive maintenance, automated work orders, and compliance-by-design.',
    343: 'A static, offline virtual testbed without live data or actuation; the optimal flight scheme conclusion is case-specific and simplified, damage comes from assumed seismic analysis, and no automated damage detection is yet implemented. Future development includes component-level FE analysis, part and texture libraries for automated CG modeling, multi-UAV path planning, and machine-learning damage detection trained on synthetic images.',
    347: 'The arm keeps a fixed pose while its base moves, execution halts and waits for humans when obstacles appear, material positions are assumed known, and point-cloud processing causes delays; verification is mostly simulated rather than on a real site. Future work targets dynamic arm pose adjustment, autonomous path adaptation, vision-based material detection, real-time performance, and long-term human factors studies on physical KUKA KR120 arms.',
    349: 'Laboratory-only validation on a 1:2 scale with one slow robot at 3 to 7 percent speed, AprilTag localization errors causing collisions at 1 mm gaps, manually authored BIM sequence and gripping data, and no support for deformable or fluid materials. Future work includes continuous component tracking, a second arm with vacuum gripping, computational design of fabrication data, force-feedback control, and efficiency studies.',
    354: 'Entirely conceptual with no implemented system, case study, or quantitative validation; the framework and its service-oriented construction platform remain unbuilt. Future work stated by the author targets scalable and interoperable digital twin systems, expansion of AI-driven learning models, and validation through large-scale pilot applications.',
    357: 'Object localization suffers uncorrected perspective and lens distortion effects, virtual-to-real alignment is manual, the detector covers only person and truck classes from MS-COCO, and turning vehicles expose uncovered red zones. Future work includes distortion correction, image-based prediction for fast-moving hazards, additional IoT sensors, spatial-anchor based automatic alignment, and cognitive ergonomics evaluation of user workload.',
    358: 'Generalization to abrupt or unseen geological transitions is limited because the model learns only from historical data, it lacks physical interpretability, and expert-based parameter selection remains subjective; control instructions are executed by human operators rather than automated actuation. Future research will embed geological priors and governing physical equations into the network so it can self-correct on sudden ground changes.',
    359: 'The three studied soils are relatively uniform, so complex ground behavior is untested, penetration degree and tool size are ignored, and real-time monitoring data must be imported manually with no autonomous platform link. Future work will add more shield projects and soil types for generalizability and connect the monitoring platform so prediction and optimization run independently.',
    360: 'Camera position and attitude must be calibrated one by one, two-way interaction between the virtual and real models is not yet realized, and the video data structure algorithm lacks integration; field cameras have low resolution and incomplete coverage. Future work includes online data-driven 3D scene updates, data-driven traffic operation simulations, and predictive deduction.',
    361: 'The platform is a monitoring and visualization system without predictive analytics or actuation, validated on only one waterway segment; future work focuses on digital twin scene iteration driven by online data, simulation and fusion drawing of water traffic operation, and updating of the water environment from monitoring data.',
    366: 'The model is offline-trained on numerical simulation data and the advance forecast is less precise than reconstruction, with up to 18% error in one experimental scenario; future work refines ADLSTM-Fire for unfamiliar buildings, adds building layout as an input parameter, enriches datasets with structural and wind factors, optimizes sensor layouts, and tests more building types.',
    368: 'Localization reaches only zonal level with about one floor of error because adjacent-floor signatures are similar; the method covers only single-frequency steady-state excitations, edge nodes run only basic signal processing, and validation used one building with five sensors. Future work targets floor-specific identification, multi-source non-stationary vibration, and deep learning at the edge.',
    372: 'Tie-point selection is manual and the separate merging programs take about 25 minutes to run; the fusion lacks level-of-detail handling which slows BIM loading, the structural safety evaluation function is reserved and not yet developed, and dynamic analysis of overall building health from local sensor data requires further investigation.',
    376: 'Overlapping personnel and machinery cause incomplete information capture, extreme lighting degrades stability (Type S3 precision fell to 73.97% under overexposure), and the vision system works only within about 20 meters, excluding high-rise and large buildings; future work adds multiple perspectives against occlusion and tests update frequencies.',
    377: 'The motion prediction model is trained on the Human3.6M laboratory dataset, creating a generalization gap to real construction postures; occlusions, lighting variability, and camera positioning limit reliability, and validation covered only three relatively simple high-risk zones. Future work adds more sensor types, lightweight edge-distributed architectures, domain-adaptive learning, and broader site validation.',
    379: 'The closed loop is human-machine collaborative, with operators filtering algorithm outputs rather than autonomous actuation, optimization takes about 900 seconds per ring, and validation is limited to one 100-ring subsection of a single project; future work includes transfer learning across geological conditions, improved sensing, and operator training programs.',
    382: 'Nuanced anomalies such as gradual tilt drift require offline post-processing rather than live dashboard analytics; air quality sensors lost up to 30.65% of expected records and one water sensor never transmitted; only one site and asset type was validated. Future work embeds predictive analytics in the live platform, adds buffering and failover mechanisms, and extends validation to bridges and tunnels.',
    386: 'The virtual simulation lacks detailed display and monitoring of worker behavior, health, and collision risks, and pre-construction risk analysis is not integrated; future work adds more monitoring data types, deeper pre-construction risk analysis, and an improved tunnel construction information database for predictive analysis in the maintenance stage.',
    388: 'Evaluation is entirely numerical on synthetic 2D datasets with single circular anomalies; the parameterization restricts detection to predefined shapes, spectral truncation distorts geometry, and the simulation-to-reality gap leaves field deployment untested. Future work adopts level-set representations, synchrosqueezed wavelet transforms, and libraries of condition-specific operators.',
    389: 'Validation is confined to one open-pit mine backfill condition and the authors state more practical tests are needed to verify reliability; blade paths still depend on expert operator knowledge. Future work continues optimizing the system, improving algorithm accuracy and reliability, and advancing intelligent mine construction.',
    396: 'Static geometric twin only: DS-gDT cannot monitor component stresses or strains or update joint positions in real time, point cloud processing is time-consuming, and clustering accuracy drops when paired regions lack data. Authors plan to extend the method to suspend-dome and reticulated shell structures, build a mechanical twin and quantify how joint deviations affect structural stability.',
    398: 'Validated on a scaled tower crane model plus one Xiangyang construction project, so generalizability is limited by the small sample size; impact on situation awareness was not systematically measured and testing scenarios may not capture real-world diversity. Future work includes integrating structural health monitoring and augmented reality into the platform.',
    401: 'Operates near real time without continuous streaming or IoT data links, needs substantial computation and memory, and accuracy degrades under extreme occlusion or reflective surfaces. Authors plan to support diverse BIM standards and city-scale asset portfolios, integrate IoT live monitoring and automated UAV deployment, and enrich semantic defect reporting for maintenance scheduling.',
    402: 'Conceptual framework without a completed application case, so overall performance improvement cannot be quantified; validation relies on 31 questionnaires and 10 interviews, which the authors note are limited by time and resources. Future directions include autonomous feedback and control from twin to physical world, human-in-the-loop research, and governance and ethics of twin data.',
    404: 'Validated only on a scale model with four electric actuators instead of the real 12-cylinder hydraulic system; preset loading means failure boundaries, wind, actuator saturation, sensor drift and communication latency were not explored, and the twin has a 1-1.5 second delay. Future work targets stress-strain sensors, finite element safety assessment, real ABM operational data and physics-informed neural networks.',
    405: 'The actual bridge was still under construction and rotation had not started, so verification is limited to a 1:100 scale model and the design decomposition phase; the authors acknowledge implementation costs, resource needs, system complexity and applicability constraints. Future research targets standardization frameworks, integrated toolchains and machine learning for long-term deformation and predictive maintenance.',
    408: 'Quantification depends on an approximately equal-distance imaging assumption that weakens in complex geometries with occlusion, the dataset covers only cracks and spalling from one regional context on concrete facades, and no temporal defect progression data exists. Future work will extend defect categories, facade materials and environments, reduce distance dependence and add repeated observations for deterioration analysis.',
    412: 'Validation uses physical models rather than a live construction site; when dangerous or warning zones are misjudged as safe the system lacks a dynamic response mechanism, and black-box deep models plus sensor limits can compromise recognition. Future work adds a dynamic verification module, thermal, UWB and lidar sensors, model interpretability and edge-cloud reliability improvements.',
    413: 'Geological modelling uses a coarse grid due to sparse data, step durations are recorded manually giving static probability distributions, sensing relies on subjective manual measurement, and the twin exerts only indirect control without real-time feedback to machinery. Future work covers tunnel seismic prediction and GPR data, 24-hour cameras for dynamic parameter updates, IoT sensor networks and unmanned construction.',
    414: 'Simulations assume vehicles cross individually, ignoring queues and congestion; training multiple Transformers for many measurement points burdens real-time use; prediction accuracy depends on finite element models; and validation is limited to box girder bridges. Future work includes realistic traffic models with generative augmentation, transfer learning, periodic load tests for model updating and other bridge types.',
    416: 'Only vault settlement is verified, on a single Grade-V rock tunnel section with data collected once per day, so real-time continuous mapping is not demonstrated and assessment of other risk types remains theoretical. Authors state they will verify the method across as many security risk categories as possible to strengthen the theory.',
    418: 'A retrospective forensic tool: the accident has already occurred and caused heavy losses, and the twin is built from drawings and records rather than live sensor data. Future research will establish digital twin models for important buildings in advance to perform multihazard simulations and continuously monitor key component mechanical states to prevent disasters.',
    420: 'The index selection in the construction process is not comprehensive enough and the data collection area is narrow, which the authors state affects universality; the work remains a modelling study without a demonstrated live sensor-to-twin data link. Future work will select multilevel data, supplement research data, and reduce the deviation of research results.',
    421: 'The BP network is trained only on finite element simulation data, only two mechanical parameters are predicted, and validation covers a single string beam of one convention center roof; no online updating from live monitoring is implemented. Future research will combine mechanical with design parameters to find key safety factors and consider more realistic conditions.',
    423: 'Evaluation baselines rely only on historical monitoring-data statistical models, without FEM simulation results, and the IFC schema still lacks dam-specific entities such as IfcDam and IfcDamFoundation; evaluation remains one-way with no actuation. Future work is integrating simulation results into the dam DT and combining both information sources.',
    426: 'Predicted structural performance and motion are only displayed on the platform without autonomous decision-making, and prediction correctness depends on sensor data accuracy. Future research will adopt deep learning for data correction, reinforcement learning for autonomous control, and cloud and blockchain strategies for data storage, cleaning, and security.',
    427: 'The framework is mostly conceptual; the paper does not describe in detail how each construction stage integrates and upgrades with the BIM-DT model, and the empirical study covers only the construction phase. Future research will focus on applying each stage of the framework in practice.',
    428: 'Safety warning distances are set from experience rather than from the uncertainty of the pipe BIM, and the excavator case is validated in one project; hardware random errors are ignored. Future work will derive reasonable warning distances through field tests and extend the pose estimation method to other heavy machinery.',
    429: 'A single case study limits generalizability; parametric objects are tailored to project-specific proprietary systems, manual steps remain due to imperfect data interoperability and missing tunnel IFC standards, and no benchmark control project allows quantifying operational savings. Future research will evaluate adaptability across projects, scalability, and standardized IFC integration.',
}
